var IT=[["Abjurer's Gilder","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A golden badge for Wizards who excel at Abjuration. Shield is always prepared for you if it is in your spellbook, and it does not count against your prepared spells. You can also cast Shield as a special Reaction when hit by an attack roll or targeted by Magic Missile. It works once per turn cycle (not again until the start of your next turn) and does not use up your normal Reaction.",{"by":"Wizard"}],["Aegis of Radiance","Armor","Rare",1,"A Shield with an extra +1 bonus to AC that serves as a Holy Symbol and shows your deity's emblem. Bonus Action with a command word: it shatters into shards of light that protect you like a held Shield and leave your hands free. The shards last 1 minute, shed Bright Light in 20 ft and Dim Light 20 ft more, and give Undead Disadvantage on attacks against you. Usable once per dawn.",{"by":"Cleric","ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"ac":1},"base":["Shield"]}],["Amulet of Equilibrium","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A three-crystal pendant that works as a Spellcasting Focus. It has 4 charges and regains 2 at dawn. When you deal Cold, Fire or Lightning damage to only one creature, spend any number of charges to reroll that many damage dice (you must use the new rolls). Taking Cold, Fire or Lightning damage from an enemy restores 1 charge.",{"ch":[4,"2","dawn"]}],["Arcane Mirror","Armor","Very Rare",1,"A Shield that holds 10 charges and regains 1d6 + 4 at dawn. Reaction when hit by an attack: cast Shield from it (once per Short or Long Rest). Reaction after you pass a save against a single-target spell or a spell attack misses you: learn its level, then spend charges equal to that level (not 7 or higher) to reflect it. The caster makes a DC 16 Dexterity save and takes 1d8 Radiant per charge spent (half on a success). If a reflected spell would have dealt half damage on a success, you take none.",{"ch":[10,"1d6 + 4","dawn"],"base":["Shield"]}],["Arcanist's Bowstaff","Staff","Very Rare",1,"A Quarterstaff that can curve into a Longbow when you attack at range. You are proficient with that bow and it lacks Heavy. It fires arcane arrows it makes itself and returns to a staff afterward. You gain +2 to attack and damage rolls and may use Intelligence for them. It has 8 charges and regains 1d6 + 2 at dawn. After an attack roll as part of the Attack action, spend 1 charge to cast Magic Missile as a Bonus Action.",{"by":"Creature with Intelligence 17 or higher","ch":[8,"1d6 + 2","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Architect's Disdain","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"An adamantine War Pick made to break walls. You gain +2 to attack and damage rolls. Every hit on an object or structure is a Critical Hit. A hit on a magically created object or structure (such as a Wall of Ice) can dispel it as Dispel Magic at level 6, but this fails if it was made with a level 7 or higher slot. Once it dispels something, it cannot do so again until the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["War Pick"]}],["Astral Bracelet","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"The base form of a family of six bracelets (Energy, Heavens, Hells, Knowledge, Omniscience, Planebending). A wondrous bangle that you can pull off and hold as a Magic action, when it unfolds into an astronomical sphere. It has 10 charges, usable only in sphere form, and regains 2d4 + 2 at dawn. Spending its last charge folds it back into a bracelet, and a Magic action folds it early. While holding the sphere you can spend charges to cast its listed spells with your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Material components costing 100 gp or more are still needed.",{"ch":[10,"2d4 + 2","dawn"]}],["Astral Bracelet of Energy","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A wondrous bangle that you can pull off and hold as a Magic action, when it unfolds into an astronomical sphere. It has 10 charges, usable only in sphere form, and regains 2d4 + 2 at dawn. Spending its last charge folds it back into a bracelet, and a Magic action folds it early. While holding the sphere you can spend charges to cast its listed spells with your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Material components costing 100 gp or more are still needed. Spells: Tenser's Floating Disk (1 charge), Dispel Magic (3), Hypnotic Pattern (3), Protection from Energy (3), Hallucinatory Terrain (4), Otiluke's Resilient Sphere (4), Globe of Invulnerability (6).",{"by":"Sorcerer or Wizard","ch":[10,"2d4 + 2","dawn"]}],["Astral Bracelet of Heavens","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A wondrous bangle that you can pull off and hold as a Magic action, when it unfolds into an astronomical sphere. It has 10 charges, usable only in sphere form, and regains 2d4 + 2 at dawn. Spending its last charge folds it back into a bracelet, and a Magic action folds it early. While holding the sphere you can spend charges to cast its listed spells with your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Material components costing 100 gp or more are still needed. Spells: Detect Evil and Good (1 charge), Protection from Evil and Good (1), Warding Bond (2), Magic Circle (3), Spirit Guardians (3), Divination (4), Dispel Evil and Good (5).",{"by":"Cleric or Paladin","ch":[10,"2d4 + 2","dawn"]}],["Astral Bracelet of Hells","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A wondrous bangle that you can pull off and hold as a Magic action, when it unfolds into an astronomical sphere. It has 10 charges, usable only in sphere form, and regains 2d4 + 2 at dawn. Spending its last charge folds it back into a bracelet, and a Magic action folds it early. While holding the sphere you can spend charges to cast its listed spells with your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Material components costing 100 gp or more are still needed. Spells: Detect Evil and Good (1 charge), Hellish Rebuke (1), Protection from Evil and Good (1), Flaming Sphere (2), Magic Circle (3), Fire Shield (4), Dispel Evil and Good (5).",{"by":"Cleric, Warlock or Wizard","ch":[10,"2d4 + 2","dawn"]}],["Astral Bracelet of Knowledge","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A wondrous bangle that you can pull off and hold as a Magic action, when it unfolds into an astronomical sphere. It has 10 charges, usable only in sphere form, and regains 2d4 + 2 at dawn. Spending its last charge folds it back into a bracelet, and a Magic action folds it early. While holding the sphere you can spend charges to cast its listed spells with your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Material components costing 100 gp or more are still needed. Spells: Comprehend Languages (1 charge), Detect Magic (1), Identify (1), Locate Object (2), Dispel Magic (3), Sending (3), Locate Creature (4), Legend Lore (5).",{"by":"Bard, Cleric, Druid, Ranger or Wizard","ch":[10,"2d4 + 2","dawn"]}],["Astral Bracelet of Omniscience","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A wondrous bangle that you can pull off and hold as a Magic action, when it unfolds into an astronomical sphere. It has 10 charges, usable only in sphere form, and regains 2d4 + 2 at dawn. Spending its last charge folds it back into a bracelet, and a Magic action folds it early. While holding the sphere you can spend charges to cast its listed spells with your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Material components costing 100 gp or more are still needed. Spells: Detect Magic (1 charge), Detect Thoughts (2), See Invisibility (2), Sending (3), Arcane Eye (4), Scrying (5), Telepathic Bond (5).",{"by":"Wizard","ch":[10,"2d4 + 2","dawn"]}],["Astral Bracelet of Planebending","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A wondrous bangle that you can pull off and hold as a Magic action, when it unfolds into an astronomical sphere. It has 10 charges, usable only in sphere form, and regains 2d4 + 2 at dawn. Spending its last charge folds it back into a bracelet, and a Magic action folds it early. While holding the sphere you can spend charges to cast its listed spells with your spellcasting ability and spell save DC. Material components costing 100 gp or more are still needed. Spells: Find Familiar (1 charge), Misty Step (2), Rope Trick (2), Sending (3), Banishment (4), Dimension Door (4), Plane Shift (7).",{"by":"Sorcerer, Warlock or Wizard","ch":[10,"2d4 + 2","dawn"]}],["Astral Sea Piercer","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A golden War Pick forged in the Astral Plane. You gain +3 to attack and damage rolls and a hit deals an extra 1d4 Force. In the Astral Plane you know the way to the nearest portal. It has 4 charges and regains 1d3 + 1 at dawn. **Portal.** Bonus Action, 1 charge: plant it in a flat surface to make a rift lasting 1 minute. A second rift within 300 ft opens a portal between them until the end of your next turn (closable early). Medium or smaller creatures and objects pass freely. **Rift Strike.** When you hit a Small or larger creature, spend 1 charge for an extra 1d8 Force and a rift on its body. When a portal opens to it, the creature makes a DC 17 Charisma save or is shunted through (Large and larger pass automatically).",{"ch":[4,"1d3 + 1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3},"base":["War Pick"]}],["Aurum and Argentum","Weapon","Rare",0,"A gold and silver pair of Daggers that become magical when used together. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls while holding one in each hand. The extra attack from the Light property can add your ability modifier to its damage. If both hit the same target in a round, the second attack deals an extra 1d4 Piercing and the target cannot make Opportunity Attacks until the end of your turn.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Dagger"]}],["Avian Circlet","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A silver tiara that gives power over flying creatures. You can cast Animal Messenger or Speak with Animals from it, but only on targets with a Fly Speed. Magic action: touch a willing Beast with a Fly Speed to see through its eyes (and use its special visual senses) for 1 minute. You can end it early. Usable once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Axe Beak Tomahawk","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Handaxe made from a slain axe beak. The first time each turn you hit a creature with a Fly Speed, it makes a DC 13 Strength save. Each failure reduces its Fly Speed by 15 ft for 1 minute.",{"base":["Handaxe"]}],["Bag of Sundrops","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A bag holding 1d6 + 4 glowing golden orbs. Magic action: throw one at a point you can see within 30 ft. It bursts into a pillar of sunlight (5-ft radius, 40 ft high Cylinder) of Bright Light that lasts until the start of your next turn. Dispel Magic on it ends it early.",{}],["Band of Mirrored Essence","Ring","Rare",1,"A mirror-polished platinum ring. When you reduce a Small or larger enemy to 0 Hit Points, use a Reaction to capture a bit of its essence (the ring holds one at a time and cannot capture again for 1d8 hours). Magic action: release it to take the creature's appearance or one feature. **Appearance.** An illusion of a creature up to one size larger or smaller, lasting 8 hours (DC 16 Intelligence (Investigation) sees through it). **Feature.** Gain one skill or save proficiency, Damage Resistance, Condition Immunity, special sense, language, or water breathing it had, for 8 hours.",{}],["Bands of the Found and Lost","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A pair of leather bracelets with compasses. While two creatures each wear one, each compass points at the other (direction only, not height or depth). They spin wildly if the bands are on different planes.",{}],["Bard-in-a-Box","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A music box. Bonus Action while holding it: command it to play a song it knows, in tinny form without lyrics, at any volume. It remembers up to five songs from sheet music (labeled with song title, page number and instrument) fed into its slot. The sheet is consumed, and a sixth song makes it forget the oldest.",{}],["Barge Helm","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A flat, rugged helmet. If you move at least 20 ft in a straight line toward a target right before you shove it, the target takes 1d6 Bludgeoning damage.",{}],["Barricade Shield","Armor","Uncommon",0,"A sturdy iron Shield. Magic action: plant it to grow up to 15 ft in height and width, fitting enclosed spaces like tunnels. While holding it expanded your Speed is 0 and you have Disadvantage on Dexterity checks and saves. It stays the same weight and becomes a nonmagical object with AC 14 and HP 40. It lasts 1 minute and reverts early if destroyed or moved (or by your Bonus Action). Usable once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"base":["Shield"]}],["Basco's Handy Bangle","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A platinum bangle with ten tool runes: Alchemist's Supplies, Calligrapher's Supplies, Carpenter's Tools, Cook's Utensils, Leatherworker's Tools, Smith's Tools, Tinker's Tools, Musical Instruments (drum, flute, lute, lyre), Navigator's Tools and Thieves' Tools. Magic action: touch a rune and say the command words to gain proficiency with that tool for 24 hours, or Expertise if already proficient. A used rune cannot be used again for 1d4 days.",{}],["Basilisk Dagger","Weapon","Rare",0,"A Dagger from a slain basilisk. It deals an extra 1d4 Poison on a hit. When you roll a 20 on an attack roll with it against a Large or smaller creature, the target makes a DC 15 Constitution save or is Restrained until the end of your next turn.",{"base":["Dagger"],"xd":["Poison: +1d4"]}],["Bath Potion","Potion","Common",0,"A frothy, lavender-scented potion. Drinking it rinses away dirt and grime and leaves your breath, hair and nails clean for 24 hours, polished or scented of daisies and honey. Bubbles escape your mouth while it lasts.",{}],["Baton of Many Sizes","Rod","Uncommon",0,"A segmented 1-ft rod. Magic action with a command word: extend it in either direction up to 50 ft, stopping when it touches a creature or surface. Beyond 10 ft it is unwieldy: at the start of each of your turns make a Strength (Athletics) check against DC 8 + 1 per 5 ft past 10, or lose your grip. Dropping it or attacking with it retracts it. The command word as a Magic action retracts it too.",{}],["Battle Tax","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A golden Battleaxe favored by merchants. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls. When you roll a 20 on an attack roll against a Small or larger enemy, you magically earn Gold Pieces equal to the attack's damage, put in your pack or purse (or sprayed from the target if you have no room). It then cannot create coins for 12 hours.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Battleaxe"]}],["Battlebrew Maul","Weapon","Rare",0,"A Maul whose head is an alchemical keg of battlebrew liquor (holds 4 gallons, makes 1 gallon at dawn and 1 more when you roll Initiative). Utilize action to detach the handle or to pour or stopper it. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls. On a 20 to hit, the target takes an extra 2d6 Acid, and the next Fire damage it takes within 1 minute deals an extra 2d6 Fire.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Maul"]}],["Battlechef Buckler","Armor","Uncommon",0,"A small Shield that was a famed chef's pot lid. While wielding it you have Advantage on saves against Fire damage. Placed face down over a pot with up to 2 gallons of water-based liquid, it brings the liquid to a boil after 10 minutes.",{"base":["Shield"]}],["Battlechef's Splendid Saucepan","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"A saucepan that turns up to 1 pound of nonmagical organic material boiled for 10 minutes or more into a stew that feeds four for a day. It works as a Mace with +1 to attack and damage rolls and deals an extra 1d4 Thunder to a target in metal armor or made of metal or stone. If you wear no Heavy armor, Utilize action to wear it as a helmet for +1 AC, or to remove it.",{}],["Belt of the Raid Leader","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A rivet-studded belt with a skull buckle. Magic action: a war cry that gives you and up to five allies within 60 ft who can hear you Advantage on attack rolls until the start of your next turn. You also make one weapon or Unarmed Strike attack as a Bonus Action. Usable once per dawn.",{"by":"Orc","ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Bird of a Feather (Common)","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A stuffed roc toy filled with enchanted down. Magic action: gain a Fly Speed of 20 ft for 1 minute or until your Concentration ends. It carries up to 200 lb. Taking damage while flying ends the effect and you fall. When the effect ends, the toy becomes nonmagical.",{}],["Bird of a Feather (Uncommon)","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A stuffed roc toy filled with enchanted down. Magic action: gain a Fly Speed of 20 ft for 1 minute or until your Concentration ends. It carries up to 200 lb. Taking damage while flying ends the effect and you fall. This version stays magical but cannot be used again for 1d4 hours, and it chirps when ready.",{"ch":[1,"1","1d4 hours"]}],["Blizzard Sphere","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A glass sphere holding a raging blizzard. Magic action: throw it at a creature or object within 30 ft to shatter it into a 20-ft-radius Emanation of ice and snow. A creature that first enters it on a turn or starts its turn there makes a DC 15 Constitution save, taking 4d8 Cold and having its Speed halved until the start of its next turn on a failure (half damage only on a success). The ground becomes Difficult Terrain and the area is Heavily Obscured. It lasts 1d4 rounds or until Dispel Magic (as a level 5 spell).",{}],["Blood Pact Pendants","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"A pair of iron pendants. You and a close ally spend a 1-minute ritual to agree on Hit Points to sacrifice, lowering both of your Hit Point maximums by that amount (minimum 1). While both wear a pendant on the same plane, when one dies it revives at once with 2d10 Hit Points plus twice the Hit Points sacrificed. The other then drops to 0 Hit Points and is Unconscious, and both maximums return to normal. This ignores effects that stop a creature from reaching 0. After this the pendants crack and lose their magic.",{}],["Bloodmage Dagger","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"An obsidian Dagger usable as a Spellcasting Focus. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls. It has 5 charges and regains 1d3 + 2 at dusk. **Blood Strike.** Magic action, 1 charge: a melee spell attack against a living creature within 5 ft deals 3d6 plus your spellcasting modifier Necrotic and heals you the same (no healing from Construct, Plant or Undead). **Blood Boost.** When you cast a level 1 to 3 spell on yourself or one creature, spend charges to raise the slot level by 1 each (max 5), and spend and roll that many Hit Point Dice, taking the total as Necrotic damage that ignores Resistance and Immunity. If it drops you to 0 Hit Points, the spell fails and you are Unconscious.",{"by":"Spellcaster","ch":[5,"1d3 + 2","dusk"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Dagger"]}],["Bloodscryer Oculus","Wondrous Item","Legendary",1,"Red goggles with magnifying lenses. You ignore visual obscurity such as fog or smoke, and see normally in Dim Light and Darkness (magical or not) out to 60 ft, or 60 ft farther if you already have Darkvision. You have Advantage on sight-based Wisdom (Perception) checks. You can cast Hunter's Mark (level 3 version), Locate Creature or Scrying (no Concentration for it) from them, but only on creatures whose blood you can see. Each spell can be used once per dawn.",{"by":"Ranger","fx":{"dark":60}}],["Bolt","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A metal Heavy Crossbow that makes its own lightning ammunition when you draw the string. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls, and it deals 1d12 Lightning instead of 1d10 Piercing. You have Advantage on ranged attacks with it against a metal target or a creature in metal armor. It also draws bolts: if another creature within 10 ft takes Lightning damage while you hold it, you take 1d6 Lightning per 10 damage that creature took.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"wp":{"d":"1d12","t":"Lightning","cat":"M","k":"R","p":"Heavy, Loading, Two-Handed","m":"Push","w":18,"r":"100/400","xw":1},"base":["Bolt"]}],["Boots of Dendallen","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"Cursed fleshy boots. You gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed and can hover up to 20 ft off the ground, and Dash moves you an extra 10 ft. They have 4 charges and regain 1d3 + 1 at dusk. Bonus Action, 1 charge: cast Expeditious Retreat or Misty Step (in dark mist). **Curse.** On first wearing, make a DC 16 Wisdom save. On a failure you take 4d8 Necrotic and cannot remove them without Remove Curse or similar magic. You then have Disadvantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks and Dexterity saves and standing up costs 10 ft extra. Removing the boots deals another 4d8 Necrotic.",{"ch":[4,"1d3 + 1","dusk"],"fx":{"fly":"walk"}}],["Boots of the Cloud Jumper","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"You can jump in midair as if from solid ground, treating it as a standing jump and never farther than your remaining movement. You can do this once before touching a solid surface again. A midair jump while falling lets you subtract up to 20 ft when calculating fall damage.",{}],["Borboss' Joyous Wand of Color","Wand","Common",0,"A prismatic crystal wand. You can draw strokes of color in midair or on any surface it touches. The drawing is illusory, visibly magical, sheds Dim Light in 5 ft and fades after 1 hour. Drawing on something worn or carried by an unwilling creature requires it to fail a DC 10 Dexterity save.",{}],["Boreal Pendant","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A floating snowflake that gives you Resistance to Cold damage and an aura of cheer. It has 8 charges and regains 1d6 + 2 at dawn. Spend charges to cast (save DC 15) Charm Person (1 charge), Color Spray (1), Hypnotic Pattern (3) or Ice Storm (4). If you spend the last charge, roll a d20. On a 1 the pendant melts, then reforms after 1 year.",{"ch":[8,"1d6 + 2","dawn"],"fx":{"res":["Cold"]}}],["Bottled Abyss","Potion","Very Rare",0,"A vial of fuming black poison. A creature that drinks it takes 4d6 Psychic and makes a DC 18 Constitution save. On a failure it is Blinded and cannot benefit from a Long Rest, and its sleep is full of nightmares. It repeats the save every 24 hours. The poison ends on a success or with Greater Restoration, Heal or Wish.",{}],["Bounty Hunter Enforcer","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Spear with a hollow head holding a spring-loaded Net. Its attacks deal Bludgeoning instead of Piercing. After a melee hit, Bonus Action: deploy the Net so a Large or smaller target is Restrained. Retracting and resetting it is a Utilize action. While it is deployed your Spear attacks have Disadvantage, and while something is Restrained by it you cannot make weapon attacks with the Spear. Bonus Action: prime it to deploy on the next hit, even thrown. A new Net takes 1 minute to attach.",{"base":["Spear"]}],["Bow of Mind Thievery","Weapon","Rare",1,"A magic Shortbow whose Arrows deal an extra 1d4 Psychic. When an Arrow hits a Humanoid, it makes a DC 15 Wisdom save or is affected by Dominate Person for up to 1 minute with no Concentration needed. You can use a Bonus Action to see and hear through the target until the start of your next turn. Usable once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"base":["Shortbow"],"xd":["Psychic: +1d4"]}],["Braided Quarterstaff","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Quarterstaff of braided rope. Bonus Action with a command word: it loosens into 50 ft of Rope, and again to tighten back. A Restrained creature held in the Rope can escape (or be freed by a creature within 5 ft) with an action and a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) check. An object up to 6 inches across tied to the end does not stop it re-forming. It can be broken only by magic, and if broken it becomes nonmagical and cannot be a staff again.",{"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Brambleheart Quiver","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A wooden Quiver that holds your Arrows and has 4 thorned magic Arrows growing on it, regrowing 1d3 + 1 picked ones at dawn. While you are attuned, you gain +2 to attack and damage rolls with them. They lose their magic 1 minute after being picked. When one hits, use a Bonus Action with a command word for 2d4 extra Piercing and Spike Growth centered within 5 ft of the target, with no Concentration, lasting until the start of your next turn.",{"by":"Druid or Ranger"}],["Breastplate of the Morning Light","Armor","Rare",1,"A Breastplate that grants +1 AC. Magic action: a blinding flash of radiant light. Other creatures within 30 ft make a DC 15 Constitution save or are Blinded until the end of their next turn. Undead have Disadvantage on the save and take 2d8 Radiant on a failure (half on a success). Usable once per dawn.",{"by":"Cleric or Paladin","ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"ac":1},"base":["Breastplate"]}],["Brooch of Many Sizes","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A dial brooch that lets you cast Enlarge/Reduce on yourself once per dawn. While it is active, Bonus Action: overload it to change size by one more category (not above Huge or below Tiny), with damage and weight changing as for a second casting. When you return to normal size after overloading, you are Incapacitated with Speed 0 until the end of your next turn, and its properties cannot be used again for 7 days.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Bug Smashers","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Gloves made from a giant centipede's barbed exoskeleton. Your Unarmed Strikes with them deal Bludgeoning or Piercing (your choice). On a 20 to hit with one, the target takes 2d6 Poison and makes a DC 13 Constitution save or is Poisoned until the start of your next turn.",{}],["Cactus Mace","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Mace with an enchanted cactus head that regrows its needles. The first target you hit with it each turn takes an extra 1d4 Piercing.",{"base":["Mace"],"xd":["First hit each turn: +1d4 Piercing"]}],["Candle of Anti-Light","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A dark candle that sheds magical Darkness in a 10-ft radius. It burns for up to 1 hour in total, and you can snuff or relight it as a Bonus Action. Covering it with something opaque blocks the Darkness. Darkvision cannot see through it and nonmagical light cannot light it up.",{}],["Catnip Amulet","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A gold and jade amulet that draws domestic cats. You have Advantage on ability checks to find or call Tiny domestic cats and on Wisdom (Animal Handling) checks to deal with them.",{}],["Celestial Circlet","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A golden circlet with a halo that sheds Bright Light in 20 ft and Dim Light 20 ft more. You are always under Protection from Evil and Good, choosing a new creature type (not Celestials) each dawn. It has 7 charges and regains 1d4 + 3 at dawn. Spend charges to cast Cure Wounds (1 per spell level, up to level 4) or Spirit Guardians (3). Before or after, use a Bonus Action to fly up to 10 ft on angelic wings with no Opportunity Attacks. If you spend the last charge, roll a d20. On a 1 it loses its magic.",{"by":"Cleric of Good alignment","ch":[7,"1d4 + 3","dawn"]}],["Ceratopper","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"An adamantine helm shaped like a triceratops. You gain +1 AC while wearing it. If you move at least 20 ft in a straight line then hit with an Unarmed Strike using it, the hit deals 3d4 plus your Strength modifier Piercing, and a target no more than one size larger makes a DC 13 Strength save or is Prone. You can also cast Polymorph from it to become a Triceratops, then not again for 2 days.",{"fx":{"ac":1}}],["Charlatan's Wardrobe","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Plain, comfortable, always clean and lightly perfumed clothes. Magic action: twirl and speak a command word to change their appearance as an illusion. A creature that takes a Study action can see through it with a DC 13 Intelligence (Investigation) check, and touching it reveals the illusion. They give no extra protection and can only look like clothes.",{}],["Chillspike","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A Pike with a never-melting ice spike. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls and a hit deals an extra 1d10 Cold. It ignores Resistance to Cold. When you reduce a Large or smaller creature to 0 Hit Points, you can entomb it in ice for 1 minute (it cannot be Prone and makes no Death Saves, ice AC 12, HP 20, immune to Poison and Psychic, vulnerable to Fire, and it crumbles if healed or destroyed). **Everglacier's Fury.** Magic action: plunge it into the ground to raise icy spikes under up to three targets within 20 ft. Each makes a DC 16 Dexterity save or takes 2d8 Cold.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Pike"],"xd":["Cold: +1d10"]}],["Chromacloth","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A silken cloth in red, yellow, green or blue, which you can change with a Magic action. The first time you take damage of the color's type while wearing it, you have Resistance to that damage, then not again until dawn. It can also be a Sling, whose ammunition deals the color's type instead of Bludgeoning. Red is Fire, yellow Lightning, green Poison and blue Cold.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"base":["Sling"]}],["Cinnabar Rapier","Weapon","Rare",0,"A Rapier coated in toxic cinnabar. It has 10 charges and regains 1d8 + 2 at dawn. When you hit, spend 1 or more charges to deal an extra 1d4 Poison per charge.",{"ch":[10,"1d8 + 2","dawn"],"base":["Rapier"]}],["Circlet of the Huntsman's Third Eye","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A barbed circlet with a preserved eye. You have Advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks. It has 5 charges and regains all at dusk. Bonus Action, 1 charge: cast Hunter's Mark, with Advantage on Constitution saves to keep Concentration on it. Spend 1 charge as a Bonus Action (or 1 more when casting Hunter's Mark) for Truesight 120 ft for 1 minute. **Curse.** Attuning curses you until Remove Curse or similar magic, and while cursed you take 1d6 Psychic whenever you roll a 1 on an attack roll or ability check.",{"ch":[5,"all","dusk"]}],["Cloak of the Boundless Spirit","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A translucent cloak that bolsters allies. It has 3 charges and regains all at dawn. Reaction, 1 charge: when an ally you can see within 15 ft takes damage, reduce it by 2d6. When an ally within 15 ft rolls 19 or 20 on a Death Saving Throw it regains 1 Hit Point, and you can spend a Reaction and 1 charge to give them 2d6 Temporary Hit Points. An ally can gain the 1 Hit Point from a 19 only once per Long Rest.",{"ch":[3,"all","dawn"]}],["Clockwork Faefly","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A 2-inch brass faefly. Bonus Action: tap it twice and it hovers 5 ft up, following you within 60 ft. It has AC 10, HP 10, Immunity to Poison and Psychic, and Resistance to other damage, and it is an object. While it flies, Bonus Action: move it 20 ft. If you are within 60 ft, Magic action: make it shine as Light or cast Faerie Fire (DC 13) in a 20-ft Cube from it, with no Concentration. Faerie Fire is usable once per dawn. Mending heals it 2d6, and at 0 Hit Points it is unusable for 2 days.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Clockwork Healerbee","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A 2-inch brass and glass bee that hovers at your side. It has 8 charges and regains 1d6 + 2 at dawn. While it is in your space, Bonus Action with a command word and up to 3 charges: it heals a creature you can see within 20 ft for 1d6 Hit Points per charge, with a burst of Bright Light, then returns. It has AC 15, HP 10, Immunity to Poison and Psychic, and Resistance to other damage, and it is an object. Mending heals it 2d6, and at 0 Hit Points it is unusable for 24 hours.",{"ch":[8,"1d6 + 2","dawn"]}],["Clockwork Inkbeetle","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A 1-inch mechanical beetle. Set on parchment you carry and it draws a to-scale map of your journey in permanent ink, even inside a book, always knowing north. Magic action: turn its dial to choose 20 ft, 200 ft, 2 miles or 20 miles per inch. It is immune to effects that change its sense of direction and stamps a compass rose first. Attached to a Band of the Found and Lost while you wear the other, it tracks you from afar on the same plane.",{}],["Coil Crook","Staff","Uncommon",0,"A red staff of rigid silk rope that is a Spellcasting Focus. Bonus Action with a command word: it becomes a 10-ft Rope, and again to return. Either form is a Focus. You can cast Rope Trick from it, using it as the rope. Usable once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Coldsnap","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Whip with +1 to attack and damage rolls that deals an extra 1d4 Cold on a hit. It has 3 charges and regains all at dawn. When you hit a creature without Cold Immunity, spend 1 charge to force a DC 15 Constitution save. On a failure its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn, and on a success its Speed is halved.",{"ch":[3,"all","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Whip"],"xd":["Cold: +1d4"]}],["Companion's Band","Wondrous Item","Common",1,"A woven band. Magic action: summon a spectral Small or smaller Beast companion (dog, cat, bird or similar) within 5 ft. It sheds Dim Light in 5 ft, stays within 30 ft of you, is Friendly, and is a magical creation (not a creature) that cannot speak. After 7 days in a row of staying or being summoned, the band links to you: it no longer needs attunement, no one else can attune to it, you summon as a Bonus Action, and the companion can be touched.",{}],["Container of Heat and Frost","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A 1-gallon iron container with three glyphs on its lid. Magic action: press one to boil the liquid (212 F), chill it (33 F), or hold its temperature between 33 and 212 F. Boiling or chilling takes 1 minute, pressing again stops it early, and the temperature then holds.",{}],["Coralshield Golem","Armor","Uncommon",1,"A crablike golem of light magical coral worn on your back. Bonus Action: it crawls down your arm and becomes a Shield, and another Bonus Action returns it to your back. If you have no free hand and will not drop what you hold, it reattaches to your back.",{"base":["Shield"]}],["Couatl Herald's Guard","Armor","Uncommon",1,"A yew Shield covered in couatl feathers. Reaction: when a creature you can see within 10 ft takes damage, you take it instead and the damage becomes Force. Usable once per Short or Long Rest. **Flight of the Couatls.** While you are attuned to three items with this property, you gain a Fly Speed of 30 ft, or 30 ft more if you already have one.",{"by":"Creature of Good alignment","ch":[1,"1","short"],"base":["Shield"]}],["Couatl Herald's Lash","Weapon","Rare",1,"A feathered Whip with its weight cut and the Light property, plus +1 to attack and damage rolls. Once each turn when you take the Attack action, you can give up one attack to bind a Medium or smaller creature in reach. It makes a DC 15 Dexterity save or is Grappled and takes 1d4 Bludgeoning. A Grappled target failing again is Restrained. It can end this with an action and a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check, or by moving over 10 ft away or by you dropping the Whip. **Flight of the Couatls.** Attuned to three such items, you gain a Fly Speed of 30 ft (or +30 ft).",{"by":"Creature of Good alignment","fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Whip"]}],["Couatl Herald's Mantle","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A cloak given to the kindhearted by a Celestial. You have Advantage on saves to avoid or end the Poisoned condition and magical contagions, and are immune to effects that sense your emotions. **Flight of the Couatls.** Attuned to three such items, you gain a Fly Speed of 30 ft (or +30 ft).",{"by":"Creature of Good alignment"}],["Couatl Herald's Radiance","Staff","Rare",1,"A wooden staff made by a couatl, with 5 charges that return 1d3 + 2 at dawn. Spend 1 charge to cast Create Food and Water, Cure Wounds (level 2), Lesser Restoration, Protection from Poison, Sanctuary or Shield with your spellcasting ability and save DC. If you spend the last charge, roll a d20. On a 1 it vanishes forever. **Flight of the Couatls.** Attuned to three such items, you gain a Fly Speed of 30 ft (or +30 ft).",{"by":"Creature of Good alignment","ch":[5,"1d3 + 2","dawn"],"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Couatl Herald's Scales","Armor","Rare",1,"Scale Mail of couatl scales. It gives +1 AC and does not impose Disadvantage on Stealth checks. **Tooth and Scale.** Reaction when a creature within 10 ft damages you: a spectral couatl strikes it. It makes a DC 15 Dexterity save and takes 4d10 Radiant on a failure, or half on a success. Usable once per dawn. **Flight of the Couatls.** Attuned to three such items, you gain a Fly Speed of 30 ft (or +30 ft).",{"by":"Creature of Good alignment","ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"ac":1},"base":["Scale Mail"]}],["Cratering Quarterstaff","Weapon","Very Rare",0,"A stony, ember-warm Quarterstaff that needs Strength 17 or higher to wield well. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls. It has 5 charges and regains 1d4 + 1 at dawn. Once per turn right after an attack roll with it, spend 1 charge (no action) to slam it into the ground, making a 10-ft Cone of tremors and flame toward the target. Each creature in it makes a DC 16 Dexterity save (the target has Disadvantage) and takes 1d8 Bludgeoning and 1d8 Fire on a failure, or half on a success.",{"ch":[5,"1d4 + 1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Crosier of Divine Power","Staff","Very Rare",1,"A staff wielded as a Quarterstaff with +3 to attack and damage rolls. When you roll Initiative against an enemy it makes 2 motes of holy power, and at the start of each combat turn roll a d6, and on a 6 a new mote appears. When you hit with it or heal with a spell or effect while holding it, spend 1 mote to add 2d6 to the damage (Radiant) or healing. A mote lasts 1 minute.",{"by":"Cleric or Paladin","fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3},"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Crown of Deep Winter","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"An icy crown from the Everglacier that gives you Resistance to Cold damage. You can cast Fire Shield from it using the chill shield option, once per dawn. **Frozen Burst.** Reaction when a creature you can see within 5 ft hits you with an attack roll: icicles burst out. Other creatures within 5 ft make a DC 16 Dexterity save and take 2d8 Cold on a failure, or half on a success. Usable once per Short or Long Rest.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"res":["Cold"]}}],["Crypt Keeper Glaive","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A Glaive with +3 to attack and damage rolls. When you reduce a Small or larger Hostile creature to 0 Hit Points with it, you gain 1d10 Temporary Hit Points and the blade glows green. Your next melee hit with it deals extra Necrotic damage equal to those Temporary Hit Points. The haze and leftover Temporary Hit Points vanish after 1 minute. Undead it kills cannot be raised again. **Six Feet Under.** The first time each turn you hit a Prone target with it, it deals maximum damage.",{"fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3},"base":["Glaive"]}],["Dagger of the Ogre Mage","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"An ogre's dagger that is large enough to be a Shortsword. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls. Its hollow hilt holds up to three Spell Scrolls. A cantrip scroll left inside for 1 minute lights one of three gems, and you can then cast that cantrip at will with your spell save DC and attack modifier, using the sword as a Spellcasting Focus that can also supply Somatic components. The scrolls do not crumble. When a damage cantrip is cast this way, the sword's damage type becomes the cantrip's for 1 minute or until you end it.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Shortsword"]}],["Couatl Herald's Fang","Weapon","Rare",1,"Any sword or dagger, forged by or from the scales of a couatl. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls. When you roll a 20 to hit, the target takes an extra 2d6 Poison and makes a DC 15 Constitution save. On a failure it is Incapacitated with Speed 0 until it takes damage or another creature uses an action to shake it out of the stupor. **Flight of the Couatls.** Attuned to three such items, you gain a Fly Speed of 30 ft (or +30 ft).",{"by":"Creature of Good alignment","fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1}}],["Couatl Herald's Reach","Weapon","Rare",1,"Any bow carved like a couatl. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls. It has 4 charges and regains 1d3 + 1 at dawn. When you make a ranged attack against a Large or smaller creature, pick a limb and spend 1 charge. A hit deals Radiant damage instead, and the target makes a DC 15 Dexterity save or the limb is pinned for up to 1 minute. The GM decides whether it falls Prone, cannot move or attacks with Disadvantage. The target or a creature within 5 ft can free it with an action and a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) check. **Flight of the Couatls.** Attuned to three such items, you gain a Fly Speed of 30 ft (or +30 ft).",{"by":"Creature of Good alignment","ch":[4,"1d3 + 1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1}}],["Dark Fathom Armor","Armor","Very Rare",1,"Sea-soaked Studded Leather covered in eldritch runes. You gain +1 AC and can breathe underwater. You can cast Evard's Black Tentacles (save DC 15) from it, centered on you as a 15-ft square that does not follow you. It needs no Concentration and you are immune to it. Usable once per dusk.",{"ch":[1,"1","dusk"],"fx":{"ac":1},"base":["Studded Leather Armor"]}],["Dead Ringer","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A bronze mask that rings when struck. When you drop to 0 Hit Points or fail a Death Saving Throw while wearing it, the three enemies nearest you within 30 ft make a DC 15 Wisdom save or take 2d12 Necrotic. A target at full Hit Points or Deafened automatically succeeds. If you are healed or stabilized after dropping to 0, it cannot be used again until the next dusk.",{}],["Death Knell","Weapon","Rare",1,"A grimly ornate Halberd with +2 to attack and damage rolls. Once per turn when you reduce a Small or larger creature to 0 Hit Points with it, a gonglike sound rings out. Each enemy within 15 ft of the target that is missing any Hit Points makes a DC 15 Wisdom save and takes 1d8 Psychic on a failure, or half on a success.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Halberd"]}],["Devil's Detail Eyepatch","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A leather eyepatch with an illusory embroidered eye that moves as you look around. Worn over an eye, whether you lack one or not, you see through the patch as through a working eye. Bonus Action with a command word: gain Darkvision 60 ft for 1 hour (60 ft more if you already have it) and see through magical Darkness as if nonmagical. Usable once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Direstone Dwarven Pick","Weapon","Rare",1,"A weathered War Pick that breaks and molds stone. You gain +2 to attack and damage rolls, and stone creatures and objects it hits take an extra 1d8 Piercing. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 at dawn. Spend 1 charge to cast Meld into Stone or Stone Shape.",{"by":"Dwarf","ch":[3,"1d3","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["War Pick"]}],["Discordant Thunderstave","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A hollow Quarterstaff with +1 to attack and damage rolls that also has the Finesse property. When you hit and roll the maximum on the weapon's damage die, roll that die again and add it as Thunder damage.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Doodle Ring","Ring","Common",0,"A wooden ring always smeared with charcoal, ink or paint. Touch the finger to a solid surface and draw as with charcoal, an ink quill or a brush (your choice), in any color. Marks smudge or wash off without a trace and fade after 24 hours. It can hold 5 square feet of drawing, and drawing more erases the earliest marks.",{}],["Doomsday Cookie","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A black sugarpaste cookie with a blank paper strip inside. Breaking it open shows a vague prediction of how you will die. Roll 1d20 on its table (for example, 1 is fiery passions, 9 is a fine meal, 20 is rocks falling). Once your death is predicted, every later cookie shows the same result for you. If you die in the foretold manner (GM's call), the paper becomes a Spell Scroll of Revivify usable only on you, and it crumbles into flour after 1 minute. The cookie is also a sweet, salty, smoky snack.",{}],["Dragon Edge Weapon","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A simple Piercing or Slashing weapon forged from a fallen dragon's claw or tooth, giving +1 to attack and damage rolls. The first time each turn you hit with an attack roll you had Advantage on, it deals an extra 1d6 damage of the type of the dragon's breath weapon. Young dragons give Uncommon weapons, adults Rare and ancient Very Rare, with a bonus set by rarity.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"xd":["Hit with Advantage: +1d6 (dragon breath type)"]}],["+1 Dragon Edge Weapon","Weapon","Rare",0,"A simple Piercing or Slashing weapon forged from a fallen dragon's claw or tooth, giving +1 to attack and damage rolls. The first time each turn you hit with an attack roll you had Advantage on, it deals an extra 1d6 damage of the type of the dragon's breath weapon. Young dragons give Uncommon weapons, adults Rare and ancient Very Rare, with a bonus set by rarity.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"xd":["Hit with Advantage: +1d6 (dragon breath type)"]}],["+2 Dragon Edge Weapon","Weapon","Very Rare",0,"A simple Piercing or Slashing weapon forged from a fallen dragon's claw or tooth, giving +2 to attack and damage rolls. The first time each turn you hit with an attack roll you had Advantage on, it deals an extra 1d6 damage of the type of the dragon's breath weapon. Young dragons give Uncommon weapons, adults Rare and ancient Very Rare, with a bonus set by rarity.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"xd":["Hit with Advantage: +1d6 (dragon breath type)"]}],["+1 Dragonkin Weapon","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Melee weapon of scaly metal that radiates draconic elements. A hit deals an extra 1d6 damage of the type of your Dragonborn Breath Weapon, and while attuned your Breath Weapon save DC rises by the same bonus. Its metal takes on your natural colors once you attune. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls.",{"by":"Dragonborn","fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"xd":["Breath Weapon type: +1d6"]}],["+2 Dragonkin Weapon","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Melee weapon of scaly metal that radiates draconic elements. A hit deals an extra 1d6 damage of the type of your Dragonborn Breath Weapon, and while attuned your Breath Weapon save DC rises by the same bonus. Its metal takes on your natural colors once you attune. You gain +2 to attack and damage rolls.",{"by":"Dragonborn","fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"xd":["Breath Weapon type: +1d6"]}],["+3 Dragonkin Weapon","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A Melee weapon of scaly metal that radiates draconic elements. A hit deals an extra 1d6 damage of the type of your Dragonborn Breath Weapon, and while attuned your Breath Weapon save DC rises by the same bonus. Its metal takes on your natural colors once you attune. You gain +3 to attack and damage rolls.",{"by":"Dragonborn","fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3},"xd":["Breath Weapon type: +1d6"]}],["Acidlight Ammunition","Weapon","Rare",0,"Any ammunition coated in an alchemical mix that ignites on impact, shedding Bright Light in the target's space and Dim Light in a 5-ft Emanation for 1 minute. A creature hit takes 1d4 Acid at the start of each of its turns and has Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks while it stays lit. The piece stays lodged until a creature uses a Utilize action to remove and snuff it, the target cannot benefit from Invisible while it is lodged, and the piece is destroyed.",{}],["Battlement Bow","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"Any bow with passive Abjuration wards. When you hit a creature with a ranged attack, a thin barrier of magic stays between you and it until the start of your next turn. Hitting a different creature moves the barrier to the new target. Against the creature the barrier guards you from, you have Half Cover against its ranged attacks and effects that originate from it.",{}],["Dragon Tamer Lance","Weapon","Legendary",1,"An iridescent Lance with +1 to attack and damage rolls that teaches you Draconic while attuned. It has 8 charges and regains 1d4 + 4 at dawn. When you hit, spend 1 charge for an extra 3d6 Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning or Poison. A Dragon hit this way also makes a DC 17 Wisdom save or is Frightened until the start of your next turn. After spending a charge you can spend a second for 1d6 more of the same type, and the target cannot take Reactions until the start of its next turn. **Wyrmling Steed.** Cast Find Steed from it once per dawn, optionally summoning a dragon wyrmling (no breath weapon, counts as one size larger when ridden) for charges equal to its CR (max 2), with matching alignment. **Forceful Impact.** Moving 20 ft in a line toward a Medium or smaller target within 5 ft gives Advantage on the melee attack, and a hit allows an extra attack against a different target directly behind it within 5 ft and not behind Cover.",{"ch":[8,"1d4 + 4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Lance"]}],["Dragon Turtle Shield","Armor","Rare",0,"A Shield of dragon turtle shell with a brass turtle head that makes and heats a small reservoir of water each dawn. Reaction when you take Fire damage while holding it: say a command word to superheat the water and halve that damage. The water bursts into a stationary cloud of steam, a 45-ft-diameter Emanation around you that is Heavily Obscured for 1 minute (or until a strong wind disperses it). The reservoir then stays empty until dawn, or until the Shield spends 1 hour in nonmagical salt water.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"base":["Shield"]}],["Dragon's Call","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"An ear cuff that teaches you Draconic while you wear it. You also get +1 to Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma checks about dragon lore.",{}],["Dragon-Kindled Edge","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A longsword made from an ancient dragon's remains. +3 to attack and damage rolls, +2d6 damage against Dragons, and you know Draconic.\n**Kindled Cleave.** Reaction when a hostile dragon's breath affects you: the blade splits it, sparing you and everything in a 30 ft Cone behind you. Once per dawn. If the breath dealt damage, the blade glows for 1 minute (Bright Light 10 ft, Dim 10 ft more) and the first hit you land with it deals an extra 6d6 of the breath's damage type, ignoring Resistance and Immunity.\n**Lesser Draconic Resistance.** Once per dawn, turn a failed save into a success if you failed by 4 or less.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3},"base":["Longsword"]}],["Dream Mantle","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A short purple cape that shows illusions of faraway places. Creatures more than 30 ft away have Disadvantage on sight-based Perception checks to spot you and on ranged attacks against you. This stops while you are Incapacitated, Restrained or unable to move. You can cast Dream (DC 16) from it over 1 minute, as the messenger. After that, wait 7 days.",{"ch":[1,"1","7 days"]}],["Druidic Throwing Club","Weapon","Rare",1,"A club with the Thrown property (range 20/60). +1 to attack and damage rolls. You know Shillelagh, and the spell does not end when you throw the club. After a ranged attack with it, the club flies back to your hand.",{"by":"Druid or Ranger","fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Club"]}],["Dryadleaf","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A plant with up to four leaves that sways as if in a breeze. As a Magic action, eat a mature leaf to speak with Beasts, Plant creatures and nonmagical plants for 1 minute. A picked leaf lasts 7 days. Potting it needs a DC 15 Intelligence (Nature) or Wisdom (Survival) check or the plant dies. It regrows 1d4 leaves every 7 days with light watering and sun.",{}],["Eaglereign","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A feathered glove. As a Magic action, cast Find Familiar from it with an Eagle form. Once per dawn.\n**Summon Giant Eagle.** Focus for 1 hour to call a Giant Eagle within 30 ft. It is your ally, acts right after you, obeys verbal commands, and carries 480 lb at 8 miles per hour. It stays 12 hours or until it drops to 0 Hit Points or you dismiss it. It can fly 9 hours per summoning, resting 1 hour per 3 hours aloft. Once it is gone, wait 2 days.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Ear Cuff of the Vampire Bat","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A ceramic bat ear cuff. When you fail a hearing-based Wisdom (Perception) check, you can command it (no action) to bite you. You take 1d4 + 1 Necrotic damage, which ignores Resistance and Immunity, and add that damage to the check.",{}],["Edible Book of Recipes","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"A recipe book that turns its pages into food. Writing a simple recipe takes 1 minute, and eating the page as a Magic action feeds you like a meal. A complex recipe takes 10 minutes to write and feeds a creature for a day. It also raises Hit Point maximum and current Hit Points by 1d10 + Proficiency Bonus until a Long Rest and lets a Poisoned or diseased eater repeat the save (once per 24 hours per creature). It works as a Spellcasting Focus for Create Food and Water.\nThe book holds 50 pages. Removing the last page or rebinding it requires a d20 roll. On a 1 the book burns into a Heroes' Feast and a 60 ft wine-and-cooking smell lasting 30 days. Otherwise rebind it with fine paper costing 5 gp per page.",{}],["Eldritch Scarf","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A wrinkled scarf with an extradimensional space (60 lb, 6 cubic feet) reachable only while worn. It always weighs 1 lb. Retrieving an item takes a Bonus Action, and its frayed hands carry up to 10 lb. Ironing it flat spills the contents. Living creatures cannot be stored. If destroyed, the contents are lost.\nAs a Magic action, use its hands for a simple task within 5 ft. They cannot attack or activate magic items. Putting it in a Bag of Holding, Portable Hole or similar item destroys both and opens a gate to the Astral Plane. Creatures within 10 ft not behind Cover are pulled through. The gate is one way and then closes.",{}],["Enchantment Breaker","Ring","Rare",0,"A ring with slowly turning chains. When healing magic such as Cure Wounds affects you, use a Reaction to repeat a save against an Enchantment spell affecting you.\n**Shatter Enchantment.** When you fail a save against an Enchantment spell, use a Reaction so you and allies within 10 ft that were targeted can reroll. Then wait 1d4 days.",{"ch":[1,"1","1d4 days"]}],["Essence of Rage","Potion","Rare",0,"Drinking it starts a 1-minute rage as the level 1 Barbarian feature, even in Heavy armor. The rage ends early if you are Incapacitated. If your turn ends without you attacking an enemy, forcing a save, or using a Bonus Action to extend it, you take 1d4 Psychic damage and the rage continues another round.",{}],["Ether Spear","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A spear with the Thrown property (20/60). +2 to attack and damage rolls and it deals Force damage. When you take the Attack action, pick a space you can see within 20 ft. The tip appears there and you can make melee attacks against a target within 5 ft of that space this turn. These attacks ignore Cover.\n**Ethereal Sight.** Bonus Action: see 60 ft into the Ethereal Plane for 1 minute. Once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Spear"]}],["Everice Box","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A 25 lb wooden box (3 ft by 2 ft by 2 ft) that keeps its contents at 40 degrees Fahrenheit and holds 24 Rations. A trapped creature is freed by a DC 10 Strength (Athletics) check from itself or someone within 5 ft. With the lid closed and latched, a Magic action and command word shrinks it to 1 ft by 8 in and halves the weight. Opening the latch restores full size. Living creatures cannot be shrunk this way.",{}],["Everlasting Sugarbomb","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A 2-inch candy that changes flavor as it dissolves. After 1 minute of dissolving, it feeds a creature for a day. It has 30 uses before it is gone. Biting to its center needs a DC 25 Strength or Constitution check, and success leads to a DC 16 Constitution save or Poisoned for 1 minute.",{"ch":[30,"0","none"]}],["Eye of Dendallen","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"Cast See Invisibility from it at will. You gain Darkvision 60 ft (or +30 ft if you had it). Bonus Action: see through magical Darkness for 1 minute, once per dusk.\n**Curse.** On attuning, make a DC 20 Wisdom save. On a success, you can end attunement at once. On a failure, or if you keep it, you tear out an eye for 4d10 Necrotic damage (none if already missing one) and the Eye takes the socket until Remove Curse. If attunement ends, it escapes as a Spider with the Undead type and 5 Hit Points. Killing it unattuned destroys it.\n**Dendallen Familiar.** Magic action: the eye crawls out and acts like a Find Familiar summon. At 0 Hit Points or when dismissed it returns, and at 0 its powers stop until dusk.",{"ch":[1,"1","dusk"]}],["Eye of the Bookwurm","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A glass sphere that finds words in writing. Bonus Action with a command word: speak a word or phrase and it floats in the sphere. Holding the eye highlights that text in green wherever you look. After the first use you can change the phrase freely for 1 hour. Then wait until dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Fable's End","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A mace. +1 to attack and damage rolls. When you roll a natural 20 against a Large or smaller creature, it makes a DC 15 Charisma save or is banished to a harmless demiplane until the end of its next turn. Against a Fey, a roll of 19 or 20 is a Critical Hit and forces the save, and the Fey has Disadvantage on it.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Mace"]}],["Ferryman's Take","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Two copper coins, heads and tails. As a Magic action, place them on the eyes of a dead, willing or Unconscious Humanoid. They do nothing unless both face the same way.\n**Heads.** An Unconscious creature becomes Stable. A conscious one enters a death-like state for 1 hour, with Immunity to Psychic damage (once per 24 hours).\n**Tails.** A dead creature gains Gentle Repose. Its body cannot be found by magic and its soul cannot be contacted.",{}],["Festerwood Buckler","Armor","Uncommon",0,"A shield with glowing amber pustules that shed Bright Light 5 ft and Dim Light 5 ft more. When a creature you can see within 5 ft misses you, use a Reaction to bash it. It makes a DC 13 Dexterity save or takes 1d4 + 1 Acid damage.",{"base":["Shield"]}],["Festerwood Claymore","Weapon","Rare",0,"A greatsword of hard festerwood with beetles inside. +1 to attack and damage rolls. On a natural 20, beetles swarm the target for 1d4 turns, dealing 1d6 Piercing at the start of each of its turns and halving its Speed. The target or a creature within 5 ft can use an action to swat them away. Against plants, Plant creatures and wooden objects the damage is maximized and lasts 4 turns.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Greatsword"]}],["Festerwood Fungal Stave","Staff","Very Rare",1,"A fungal staff with 25 charges that regains 1d10 + 15 at dusk. It needs a Cleric, Druid or Sorcerer. Magic action, spend any charges to raise that many mushroom patches within 60 ft. They are Difficult Terrain and deal 2d4 Poison per 5 ft moved. They last 1 minute or until dismissed with a Bonus Action.\nBonus Action, using your spell save DC: Fog Cloud (1), Stinking Cloud (3), Cloudkill (5) or Insect Plague (5). The spell needs no Concentration, ends at the end of your next turn and must target a point next to your mushrooms. Spending the last charge, roll d20. On a 1 the staff is destroyed and a hostile Violet Fungus grows.",{"by":"Cleric, Druid, or Sorcerer","ch":[25,"1d10+15","dusk"],"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Festerwood Logger","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A hardened festerwood handaxe. Hits deal an extra 1d4 Acid damage, maximized against plants, Plant creatures and wooden objects.",{"base":["Handaxe"]}],["Festerwood Vizard","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"An insect-like wooden mask that fits your face. You have Blindsight 10 ft. As a Magic action, beetles pour out as a Swarm of Insects (Fly Speed) that you command, moving and attacking on summoning and then as a Bonus Action each turn. If you are Incapacitated, it takes the Dodge action. It vanishes at 0 Hit Points or after 10 minutes without attacking. Once per dusk.",{"ch":[1,"1","dusk"]}],["Festerwood's Light","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A rapier inlaid with Lightspore scrapings. +1 to attack and damage rolls. You have Advantage on checks to find places in the Festerwood and Immunity to magical contagions. It sheds Bright Light 10 ft and Dim Light 10 ft more.\nMagic action with a command word: spores hit all other creatures within 30 ft. An ally can use a Reaction to attack or move up to half Speed without Opportunity Attacks. An enemy makes a DC 17 Constitution save or is Incapacitated until the end of your next turn. Once per dusk.\n**Charges.** 5 charges, regains 1d3 + 2 at dusk. Spend 1 to cast Charm Person (level 4), Compulsion, Confusion, Contagion, Faerie Fire, Locate Animals or Plants or Moonbeam (level 4), with save DC 17 and +9 to hit. You can also cast Dancing Lights. Spend 1 charge to remove a Spore Counter from a willing creature you touch.",{"ch":[5,"1d3+2","dusk"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Rapier"]}],["Fife of Dragonsong","Weapon","Rare",1,"A fife that is also a blowgun, for Bards. You are proficient with it as an instrument and as a Blowgun. +1 to attack and damage rolls and +1d6 Thunder damage on a hit.\n**Dragonsong.** Magic action, spend a Bardic Inspiration use. Enemies in a 15 ft Cone make a DC 15 Constitution save or take 2d6 Thunder damage and are pushed 10 ft (half damage on a success). Allies in the Cone who hear it gain 2d6 Temporary Hit Points and +10 ft Speed until the end of their next turn.",{"by":"Bard","fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Blowgun"],"xd":["+1d6 Thunder"]}],["Fire Dervish Cloak","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A crackling cloak with 5 charges that regains all at dawn. Once per turn, spend 1, 2 or 3 charges (no action) and lower your Speed by 10, 20 or 30 ft until the end of the turn to spin. Creatures within 5 ft make a DC 15 Dexterity save. On a failure they take 1d8 Fire per charge spent and cannot make Opportunity Attacks against you this turn.",{"ch":[5,"all","dawn"]}],["Fire Fire!","Weapon","Rare",1,"A kobold-made light crossbow with 3 charges that regains 1d3 at dawn. While it has a charge it sheds Bright Light 20 ft and Dim Light 20 ft more, and nonmagical Bolts it fires deal an extra 1d6 Fire. Magic action, spend 1 charge: a 30 ft Cone, DC 15 Dexterity save, 4d6 Fire on a failure and half on a success, and loose flammables ignite. Spending the last charge, roll d20. On a 1 the weapon turns nonmagical.",{"ch":[3,"1d3","dawn"],"base":["Light Crossbow"],"xd":["Bolts: +1d6 Fire"]}],["Fire Wand of the Unbroken Circle","Wand","Rare",1,"An ash wand for Druids with 7 charges that regains 1d6 + 1 at dawn. Cast Flame Blade (2 charges) or Produce Flame (0 charges, or 1 at level 5) with +5 to hit. Flame Blade burns above the wand instead of in your hand. If you would fail a Constitution save to keep Concentration on it, spend 1 charge as a Reaction to succeed. Spending the last charge, roll d20. On a 1 the wand burns to ash.",{"by":"Druid","ch":[7,"1d6+1","dawn"]}],["Firecracker Crystals","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A bag of 1d4 + 8 festival crystals. As a Magic action, throw one at a solid surface within 20 ft to release a harmless sensory effect that ends at the end of your turn. Roll 1d8 for each crystal for its color: 1 flame, 2 flash and citrus scent, 3 fizzing motes, 4 foul-sweet green smoke, 5 big bubbles, 6 a snippet of music, 7 glitter, 8 a mystery effect (roll again, rerolling 8s). All effects have a 5 ft reach.",{}],["Fireweaver Gloves","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"Golden gloves that let you cast Produce Flame (+5 to hit) with a 1-hour duration. You can shape that flame or other small nonmagical flames like clay for 1 minute, and a carried nonmagical flame burns for 1 hour. You can set the spell's flame down harmlessly for 1 minute (no action) and pick it up with a Magic action within 5 ft. When you take Fire damage with a free hand, use a Reaction to reduce it by 1d8 + 2.",{}],["Flesh of Dendallen","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A shirt of stitched flesh with 6 charges that regains 1d4 + 2 at dusk. Bonus Action, spend 1 charge: cast False Life. While Bloodied you regain 1d4 + Constitution modifier (minimum 1) Hit Points at the start of each turn, unless Unconscious or you took Fire or Radiant damage since your last turn began.\n**Curse.** When first worn, make a DC 20 Strength save. On a success, you can take it off. On a failure, it fuses to you and cannot be removed without Remove Curse. Nonmagical clothing beneath it is destroyed. You count as Undead as well and are Vulnerable to Radiant damage. Removing it deals 4d10 Necrotic damage.",{"ch":[6,"1d4+2","dusk"]}],["Force Gauntlet","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A jeweled gauntlet with 5 charges that regains 1d4 + 1 at dawn. When you hit with a melee attack from the gauntlet hand (weapon or Unarmed Strike), spend 1 charge for an extra 2d6 Force damage and a DC 15 Strength save. On a failure the target is pushed 10 ft away from you. On a success you are pushed 10 ft away from it. Targets two or more sizes larger than you pass automatically.",{"ch":[5,"1d4+1","dawn"]}],["Fortune's Fivepence","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"An electrum coin you can spend like an Electrum Piece. Bonus Action with a command word, within 30 ft: call it to your hand or pocket.\n**Fate Flip.** 2 charges. Once per 24 hours flip it to try to refill: heads restores all, tails none. When you carry it and a D20 Test total is 10 or lower, spend 1 charge (no action), flip a coin, and add 1d10 on heads or subtract 1d10 on tails. It does not work if the result would be 0 or lower.",{"ch":[2,"all on heads","24 hours"]}],["Fourarm Bracers","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"Bracers with 5 charges that regain 1d4 + 1 at dawn. Magic action: two spectral arms appear under your own for 1 minute. They handle objects, open doors and containers, and each carries 10 lb. Bonus Action with a command word, spend 1 charge: make two Unarmed Strikes with them using +3 Strength, your Proficiency Bonus, and 1d4 Force damage. Or spend 1 charge when summoning to double the carrying weight and make the duration 5 minutes.",{"ch":[5,"1d4+1","dawn"]}],["Fragment of Elder Starlight","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"A 3 lb egg-shaped crystal shedding sunlight in Bright Light 20 ft and Dim Light 20 ft more. A Bonus Action touch adjusts or snuffs the light. Magic action with a command word: a 60 ft Emanation of light. Undead and Fiends there not behind Cover make a DC 16 Constitution save or take 8d6 Radiant and become Blinded until the end of your next turn (half damage on a success). Chosen living allies regain 4d6 Hit Points. Once per dawn. After that, its light drops to 10 ft Bright and 10 ft Dim until then.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Frefil's Jolly Oozebean Sugarbombs","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A pack of 4 candies, with colors from 4d8 rolled when opened. Eating one is a Bonus Action and its effect lasts 1 minute. 1 White: breathe underwater. 2 Black: Resistance to Acid and can eat inedible, nonpoisonous organics. 3 Blue: grapple partners take 1d8 Acid. 4 Gray: Advantage on saves against Charmed and Frightened. 5 Gold: Climb Speed equal to your Speed. 6 Red: 1d8 + 4 Temporary Hit Points. 7 Green: Resistance to Poison and Advantage on checks to end Grappled or Restrained. 8 Yellow: Resistance to Lightning and Immunity to Magic Missile damage.\n**Upset Stomach.** Only one sugarbomb with this trait can affect you at a time. Eating a second one ends the first and forces a DC 13 Constitution save, or you are Poisoned for 1 minute.",{}],["Frefil's Tiny Tasty Tongue Twisty Sugarbombs","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A bag of 12 gumballs. As a Magic action, chew one for 5 minutes. You understand the literal meaning of any language you hear or see signed, and your accent matches the speaker's.\n**Upset Stomach.** Only one sugarbomb with this trait can affect you at a time. Eating a second one ends the first and forces a DC 13 Constitution save, or you are Poisoned for 1 minute.",{}],["Frost Giant Fork","Weapon","Rare",1,"A giant's table trident with the Thrown property (20/60). +1 to attack and damage rolls. After a melee hit, make a Bonus Action bite against the same target using Strength and Proficiency Bonus, dealing 1d6 Piercing.\n**Curse.** While attuned you must eat twice the normal amount of food and gain 1 Exhaustion level if a day passes without enough.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Trident"]}],["Frostbitten Buckler","Armor","Uncommon",1,"An icy shield with 3 charges that regains all at dawn. When a creature you can see hits you in melee, spend 1 charge as a Reaction to deal 2d4 Cold damage to it. After the attack you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the damage dealt.",{"ch":[3,"all","dawn"],"base":["Shield"]}],["Frozen Dagger","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A dagger that deals Cold damage instead of Piercing. On a natural 20, the target makes a DC 12 Constitution save or is Paralyzed until the end of its next turn. On a success its Speed is halved until then, unless it is immune to Paralyzed.",{"base":["Dagger"]}],["Funeral Marchers","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Black leather boots. When you drop to 0 Hit Points and gain Unconscious, you can choose not to fall Prone. While Unconscious and standing this way, you can walk up to 10 ft on your turn after making a Death Saving Throw.",{}],["Galea of the Soulfire Phoenix","Wondrous Item","Artifact",1,"A helmet of the phoenix hero Fara, with 7 charges that regain 1d4 + 3 at dawn. You have Resistance to Fire, and in combat harmless flames shed Bright Light 20 ft and Dim Light 20 ft more. If you die while attuned, it vanishes to the Elemental Plane of Fire.\n**Fiery Spirit.** You and allies in its Bright Light have Advantage on saves against Charmed and Frightened, and a 19 or 20 on a Death Saving Throw restores 1 Hit Point.\n**Ignite.** Bonus Action: cast Fire Shield (warm shield only) and gain flaming wings with a Fly Speed of 30 ft for the duration. Once per dawn.\n**Call of the Phoenix.** Spend charges (save DC 18) to cast Healing Word at level 2 (1), Death Ward (3) or Flame Strike (4).\n**From the Ashes.** Reaction when reduced to 0 Hit Points but not killed: drop to 1 instead, regain 14 Hit Points, and creatures within 10 ft make a DC 18 Dexterity save or take 4d10 Fire (half on a success). Wings carry you up to 60 ft away without Opportunity Attacks. Then wait 2 days.\nIt has random Artifact properties. Only an ancient phoenix eating it destroys it, and the phoenix is reborn.",{"ch":[7,"1d4+3","dawn"],"fx":{"res":["Fire"]}}],["Galvanic Steelsnare","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A steel chain Net with the Heavy property. A creature Restrained by it makes only one attack per turn. While a target within 30 ft of you is Restrained by it, use a Bonus Action and command word to shock it for 1d6 Lightning damage, or 2d6 against metal creatures or metal armor. Usable once per turn start. Escape needs an action and a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) check by the target or a creature within 5 ft (Disadvantage for Small or smaller). Destroying the Net (AC 12, 15 HP, Resistance to Slashing, Immunity to other damage) also frees it. It repairs itself in 1d6 + 1 days.",{}],["Gibberbox","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A 7 lb enamel and bone box (1 ft by 6 in by 6 in) holding the paste of a gibbering mouther. Magic action to open: a toothy mouth babbles, and touching it deals 1d6 Piercing. Each creature starting its turn within 20 ft that can hear makes a DC 10 Wisdom save. On a failure it cannot make Opportunity Attacks until its next turn and rolls d8: 1-4 does nothing, 5-6 uses all movement in a random direction with no action, 7-8 makes a melee attack on a random creature in reach. Lasts 1 minute or until closed with a Magic action. Then wait 24 hours. The paste cannot be removed.",{"ch":[1,"1","24 hours"]}],["Give and Take","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"Two scimitars joined by a chain, Give (mithral) and Take (obsidian). Your extra attack from the Light property can add your ability modifier to its damage. They share 10 charges and regain 1d6 + 4 at midday. When you hit with a blade, you can spend 1 charge for its effect.\n**Give.** You and every other creature within 5 ft of the target gain 2d6 Temporary Hit Points.\n**Take.** The target takes 2d6 Necrotic damage and you and other creatures within 5 ft of it take half as much.",{"ch":[10,"1d6+4","midday"],"base":["Scimitar"]}],["Glove of the Aegis","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A glove with 5 charges that regains 1d3 + 2 at dawn. When a target you can see hits you with an attack roll, use a Reaction and spend any number of charges to gain +2 AC per charge against that attack. It does not work while you wield a Shield.",{"ch":[5,"1d3+2","dawn"]}],["Glove of the Grim Fandango","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A glove for Bards. Worn on your dominant hand, you are proficient with all Musical Instruments. After playing for 1 minute, illusory spectral musicians join you and fade 1 minute after you stop. With them you have Advantage on Charisma (Performance) checks and +2 to your spell save DC for Enchantment spells on targets who can hear you.",{"by":"Bard"}],["Grass Carpet","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A fertile turf roll 10 ft by 5 ft with 1 inch of soil, weighing 30 lb. Plants need half the usual sun and water, and each inch of soil counts as a foot of normal soil. Folding or stacking carpets deepens the soil. It rolls up or out in 1 minute to 1 ft across. A magical blade can cut it into plots at least 1 ft on each side.",{}],["Grass Whistle Blade","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A dagger whose blade is enchanted grass with a lulling tone. +2 to attack and damage rolls. It has 4 charges and regains 1d4 at dawn. On a melee hit you can forgo the damage and spend 1 charge. The target makes a DC 16 Wisdom save or is Incapacitated until the end of its next turn, then saves again. A second failure means Unconscious for 1 minute, which ends on damage or when someone within 5 ft shakes it awake. A second success deals 3d8 Psychic damage. Creatures that do not sleep or are immune to Exhaustion automatically succeed.",{"ch":[4,"1d4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Dagger"]}],["Gravity Goblet","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A glass and silver goblet that makes liquid flow against gravity. Tilted to drink, it climbs up the cup and drops down at the rim. Swirling it makes the liquid flow the opposite way. Floating solids other than ice are unaffected.",{}],["Greaves of Dendallen","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"Skeletal greaves. You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed and can walk on liquid. Once per turn you can jump 30 ft for 10 ft of movement.\n**Curse.** When first worn, make a DC 20 Constitution save. On a success, you can take them off. On a failure, your legs break for 6d8 Necrotic damage that ignores Resistance and Immunity, and the greaves stay on until Remove Curse. The broken legs do not slow you while worn. Once removed, your Speed is 0 and rises by 5 ft every 24 hours until normal.",{}],["Grip of Dendallen","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"Gloves of bone chain. Your Unarmed Strikes deal 1d6 Necrotic damage, maximized against plants and Plant creatures. Cast Blight (Touch range), Contagion or Vampiric Touch (save DC 16, +8 to hit). Each spell can be cast once, then not again until dusk.\n**Curse.** When first worn, make a DC 16 Wisdom save. On a success, you can take them off. On a failure, chains pierce your arms for 4d6 Piercing and the gloves stay on until Remove Curse. Your hands rot with an uncontainable stench, giving you Disadvantage on Charisma checks and 1d6 Necrotic damage right after a Long Rest restores all your Hit Points. After removal, the rot takes 1d4 days to heal.",{}],["Halberd of the Peacock","Weapon","Rare",1,"A mirror-polished halberd with five gems. +1 to attack and damage rolls. It has 5 charges and regains 1d4 + 1 at dawn. Spend 1 to cast Disguise Self or 2 to cast Alter Self, Mirror Image or Shatter (save DC 15).\n**Curse.** Attuning curses you. You refuse to part with it and have Disadvantage on attacks with other weapons. When you drop a creature to 0 Hit Points with it, make a DC 12 Wisdom save or admire yourself until your next turn, losing remaining movement, action, Bonus Action and Reaction. You automatically fail Dexterity saves while admiring.",{"ch":[5,"1d4+1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Halberd"]}],["Hand of the Master","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A seamless satin glove that fits either hand and works as a missing hand or fingers. You can cast Mage Hand at will from it, with the hand appearing in the glove. This doubles the spell's duration and the weight it carries.",{}],["Harp of Valor","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A 10-string shortbow for Bards that is also a harp and a Spellcasting Focus. You are proficient with the harp and have Advantage on Charisma (Performance) checks with it. +2 to attack and damage rolls, and Arrows deal Thunder damage. It has 10 charges and regains 1d6 + 4 at dawn. Spend up to 5 charges to cast Magic Missile or Thunderwave at a level equal to the charges, with your spell save DC.",{"by":"Bard","ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Shortbow"]}],["Hasty Sugarbomb","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A sweet eaten as a Magic action to raise your Speed by 5 ft for 1 hour.\n**Upset Stomach.** Only one sugarbomb with this trait can affect you at a time. Eating a second one ends the first and forces a DC 13 Constitution save, or you are Poisoned for 1 minute.",{}],["Hat Trick","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A purple hat with 3 charges that regains 1 at dawn. While holding it, spend 1 charge to cast Find Familiar as a Magic action, as a rabbit (Weasel stats) or dove (Owl stats). It lasts 1 minute and cannot deliver spells. While wearing it you can cast Prestidigitation using only the sensory effect or minor creation (illusory image) options.",{"ch":[3,"1","dawn"]}],["Hcor'uk the Colossal's Portable Handheld Weapon of Walloping","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A flail made from a rope and a 200 lb boulder, with Heavy, Reach and Two-Handed. Hits deal an extra 1d8 Bludgeoning, or 2d8 against a structure. On a natural 20 against a Huge or smaller creature, it makes a DC 16 Strength save or falls Prone. The rope and boulder cannot be separated, and attuning makes lifting the boulder effortless.",{"base":["Flail"],"xd":["+1d8 Bludgeoning (2d8 vs structures)"]}],["Heart of the Sleeveless","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A silky vest that flatters your build and sags when taken off. Its color follows your mood: Anger red, Anticipation orange, Joy yellow, Love lime green, Fear green, Sadness navy blue, Disappointment indigo, Disgust violet, Jealousy black, Surprise white. Unworn it is a muted blue.",{}],["Hellfire Pitchfork","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A warm black iron trident weighing 10 lb with the Heavy property, so its throwing range is 15/45. +1 to attack and damage rolls and +1d8 Radiant damage on a hit. Bonus Action with a command word, while it is within 60 ft: it vanishes in smoke and appears in your open hand. If you do this right after a ranged attack, a 5 ft pillar of flame erupts in its space instead, and creatures there make a DC 16 Dexterity save or take 1d8 Fire.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Trident"],"xd":["+1d8 Radiant"]}],["Helm of Heroes","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A helmet that gives +1 AC while you wear no armor (a Shield is fine). Without armor, a natural 20 on an attack makes it glimmer for 1 minute. While it glimmers, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to half your level (rounded down) at the start of each of your turns, and you and allies within 10 ft are Immune to Frightened.",{}],["Helmsman's Shelter","Armor","Rare",1,"A shield that gives +1 AC on top of its normal bonus, and +1 to checks to control a waterborne vehicle. It has 5 charges and regains all at dawn. Spend 3 charges to cast Control Water (save DC 15). Or Magic action, spend 1 charge to seize a water vehicle with a rudder within 300 ft. A creature steering it makes a DC 15 Strength save, and on a failure you turn the vehicle up to 90 degrees and keep control until your next turn.",{"ch":[5,"all","dawn"],"fx":{"ac":1},"base":["Shield"]}],["Hexaxe","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A handaxe for Warlocks. It gives +1 to attack and damage rolls against creatures under a Concentration spell you cast as a Warlock. It has 3 charges and regains all at dusk. When you must save to keep Concentration on a Warlock spell while holding it, spend 1 charge as a Reaction to add your Charisma modifier (minimum +1).",{"by":"Warlock","ch":[3,"all","dusk"],"base":["Handaxe"]}],["Hurricane Lance","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A lance with +2 to attack and damage rolls. It has 4 charges and regains 1d4 at dawn. Magic action, spend 1 charge: surround yourself with wind for 1 minute, so you can Disengage as a Bonus Action. Spend a second charge (no action) to extend this to your mount. It ends if you are Unconscious or let go of the lance. You can also cast Thunderwave at level 3 (save DC 16) once per dawn.",{"ch":[4,"1d4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Lance"]}],["Ice Sickle","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A sickle from the Everglacier covered in regrowing icicles. The first target you hit on each of your turns takes an extra 1d6 Cold damage.",{"base":["Sickle"],"xd":["First hit each turn: +1d6 Cold"]}],["Immovable Button","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"An iron shirt button. Bonus Action with the command word \"hold\": it fixes onto unworn fabric or fabric worn by a willing creature, even against gravity. It supports 500 lb and stops tearing. More weight deactivates it. A Utilize action and DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check moves it up to 10 ft. A Study action and DC 10 Intelligence (Investigation) check shows it is magic. It holds 1 minute, and its magic is spent afterward.",{}],["Infernal Aegis","Armor","Very Rare",1,"A shield. Bonus Action with a command word: wreathe it in harmless flames (Bright Light 20 ft, Dim Light 20 ft more) until you repeat the word or let go. While holding it you have Resistance to Fire and +1 AC on top of its normal bonus. It has 4 charges and regains 1d4 at dawn. While ablaze, spend charges to cast Fire Shield (2, warm shield only) or Hellish Rebuke (1, save DC 16).",{"ch":[4,"1d4","dawn"],"fx":{"ac":1,"res":["Fire"]},"base":["Shield"]}],["Inferno Rope","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A 10 ft sulfur-smelling rope. Magic action with a command word: lay it in a line to make a 15 ft tall wall of fire along it for 1 minute (Bright Light 15 ft, Dim Light 15 ft more). Creatures other than you within 5 ft when it ignites make a DC 13 Dexterity save or take 2d4 Fire, and again on first entering the wall each turn or ending a turn in it. The rope returns afterward. Once per dawn. Only magic breaks it, and then it is a plain Rope.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Ionbreaker, the Tempest's Reach","Weapon","Artifact",1,"A longbow forged in the Stormheart storm. +3 to attack and damage rolls.\n**A Storm Is Coming.** Add 1d10 to Initiative while it is on you.\n**Fast as Lightning.** After the Attack action, make one attack with it as a Bonus Action.\n**Discharge.** After a ranged hit on your turn, the target and creatures within 5 ft take 1d8 Lightning (once per creature per round).\n**Chained Conduits.** A ranged hit makes the target a conduit for 1 minute. Bonus Action with a command word: electrify all conduits within 60 ft. Lines 5 ft wide arc between conduits within 30 ft. Each conduit takes 2d8 Lightning, others in a Line make a DC 18 Dexterity save for 2d8 (half on a success), and each can be hit once per turn.\n**Maelstrom Marksman.** Once per turn, reroll a missed ranged attack against another target within 30 ft of the first, with Disadvantage.\n**Zephyr Step.** Fly Speed equal to Speed, hovering within 20 ft of the ground.\n**Embrace the Storm.** Each time you take Lightning damage while attuned, roll 1d8: 1 Vulnerable to Lightning until your next turn end, 2 thrown 20 ft and Prone, 3 Deafened 1 hour, 4 no Reactions 1 minute, 5 Fog Cloud within 5 ft for 1d4 rounds, 6 up to three creatures within 10 ft take 1d8 Lightning, 7 double Speed until your next turn end, 8 Immune to Lightning until your next turn end.\nIt has random Artifact properties and is destroyed only by lightning and an adamantine hammer in the Stormheart, releasing 10d10 Lightning and 10d10 Force within 60 ft.",{"fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3},"base":["Longbow"]}],["Ironleaf Maul of Entanglement","Weapon","Rare",1,"A maul with a vine head. +1 to attack and damage rolls. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 at dawn. After you hit a Medium or smaller target, spend 1 charge to force a Strength save (DC 8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus). On a failure it takes 1d6 Piercing and is Restrained until the end of its next turn.",{"ch":[3,"1d3","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Maul"]}],["Ironleaf Oaken Shield","Armor","Uncommon",1,"A reinforced wooden shield for Druids. +1 AC on top of its normal bonus. It reshapes onto you when you transform into a Beast, still giving +1 AC, and returns to your arm when you revert.",{"by":"Druid","fx":{"ac":1},"base":["Shield"]}],["Ironleaf Plate","Armor","Very Rare",1,"Plate armor lined with ironleaf vines. +1 AC, it does not impose Disadvantage on Stealth, and it gives you Resistance to Bludgeoning damage. Fire damage withers the vines for 1 minute, ending these benefits. You can cast Pass without Trace once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"ac":1,"res":["Bludgeoning"]},"base":["Plate Armor"]}],["Ironshod Trotters","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"Boots with iron horseshoes. When you Dash, move 10 ft extra. Click them to cast Polymorph on yourself into a Riding Horse for 8 hours. You keep your Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma and skill and save proficiencies. Carried bags become saddlebags but other gear melds in and is unusable. Damage taken in that form carries over to your normal form and ends the spell. Once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Jotun's Jodhpurs","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Riding pants. While you wear no Heavy armor and ride a non-Humanoid mount, you count as one size smaller.",{}],["Killskull Longbow of Dread","Weapon","Rare",1,"A longbow with a bear skull. It holds up to 4 charges and gains 1 each time you drop a Small or larger creature to 0 Hit Points with it. On a ranged hit, spend 1 charge for an extra 1d8 Psychic damage and a DC 15 Wisdom save. On a failure the target is Frightened for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns.",{"ch":[4,"0","never","Gains 1 charge when you drop a Small or larger creature to 0 HP"],"base":["Longbow"]}],["Kindle Egg Sugarbomb","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A spicy chocolate sweet eaten as a Magic action. For 1 hour you have Resistance to Fire and can endure temperatures down to -50 degrees Fahrenheit without protection.\n**Upset Stomach.** Only one sugarbomb with this trait can affect you at a time. Eating a second one ends the first and forces a DC 13 Constitution save, or you are Poisoned for 1 minute.",{}],["Knight's Standard of Valor","Weapon","Rare",1,"A halberd with a flag. +1 to attack and damage rolls. You and allies within 10 ft add Proficiency Bonus to saves against or to end Frightened if not already proficient. An ally starting its turn within 10 ft gains +5 ft Speed until the turn ends. Changing the flag takes 1 hour of focus, possible during a Short Rest.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Halberd"]}],["Knight's Standard of Vigor","Weapon","Rare",1,"A brass pike with a flag. +1 to attack and damage rolls. You and allies within 10 ft add Proficiency Bonus to saves against or to end Poisoned if not already proficient. When an ally gets Hit Points from a spell or potion in combat, use a Reaction to give it an extra 1d6 + 2. Changing the flag takes 1 hour of focus, possible during a Short Rest.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Pike"]}],["Knight's Standard of Virtue","Weapon","Rare",1,"A decorated glaive with a flag. +1 to attack and damage rolls. You and allies within 10 ft add Proficiency Bonus to saves against or to end Charmed if not already proficient. When an ally you can see within 10 ft takes damage, use a Reaction to reduce it by 5 and take that much Force damage yourself. Changing the flag takes 1 hour of focus, possible during a Short Rest.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Glaive"]}],["Knocking Boots","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Dwarven steel-toed boots with a key on the toe. Kick an object that is locked or otherwise sealed against entry to cast Knock on it. Once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Kraken's Whip","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A whip made from a shrunken tentacle. Magic action: a Large or smaller creature you can see within 10 ft makes a DC 13 Strength or Dexterity save (its choice). On a failure it is Grappled and takes 1d4 + 2 Bludgeoning, and again at the end of each of its turns. Escape needs an action and a DC 13 Strength (Athletics) check by it or a creature within 5 ft. You cannot attack with the whip while grappling. You can end the grapple freely. Moving more than 10 ft away drags the target, costing you 1 extra foot per foot unless it is Tiny or two or more sizes smaller.",{"base":["Whip"]}],["Lance of the Hungering Dead","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A gruesome lance. The first time each turn you hit a living enemy in melee with it, it takes an extra 1d12 Necrotic damage and you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to half that damage (rounded up).",{"base":["Lance"],"xd":["First hit each turn on a living target: +1d12 Necrotic"]}],["Leeching Quarterstaff","Weapon","Rare",1,"A quarterstaff with +1 to attack and damage rolls. It has 6 charges and regains 1d6 at dawn. On a hit, spend 1 charge for an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage, and you regain Hit Points equal to that damage. It has no effect on Undead or Constructs.",{"ch":[6,"1d6","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Liar's Lyre","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A lyre for Bards that you are proficient with while attuned. You have Advantage on Charisma (Deception) checks when you spend at least 1 minute convincing a creature of a lie. Holding it gives +1 to your spell save DC for Vicious Mockery.",{"by":"Bard"}],["Lightning Pylons","Rod","Rare",0,"A set of three 3 ft rods tipped with blue dragon horn. Each holds an electrical charge, and a spent charge returns after 12 hours. Magic action: stand one upright within 5 ft. Bonus Action with a command word: electrify a charged pylon within 5 ft for 1 minute, after which it loses its charge. Charged pylons within 20 ft of an electrified one join it, forming an opaque 10 ft tall, 1 ft thick wall of lightning between them (up to six pylons, Bright Light 10 ft, Dim Light 10 ft more). Electrified pylons are bound to the ground.\nCreatures in the wall when it appears make a DC 15 Dexterity save (Disadvantage if metal or in metal armor), taking 5d8 Lightning and Speed 0 until their next turn on a failure, or half damage and half Speed on a success. The same save applies when first entering the wall on a turn or ending a turn within 5 ft of it. Each pylon has AC 15 and 20 HP, and is Immune to Poison and Psychic. Touching an electrified pylon or hitting it with a metal melee weapon deals 1d8 Lightning per connected pylon, itself included. At 0 HP it falls, loses its charge and cannot be used for 2 days, then it heals fully.",{}],["Locksmith's Bane","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A silver lock pick that adjusts itself to the lock. You get +3 to Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks to pick a lock with it. On a natural 1 it casts Knock on the lock and turns to dust. If you reroll or change that 1, it becomes nonmagical instead, with no spell and no dust.",{}],["Love's Embrace","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A greatsword made of two scimitars, one cold and one fire. +1 to attack and damage rolls. Two allies can attune to it together over a Long Rest, and then the bonus is +2. Bonus Action with a command word: split it into two Scimitars or rejoin it. If you hold no part of it and are on the same plane, you can summon the Greatsword or one or both Scimitars to your free hand. Separate Scimitars have the Thrown property (20/60) and deal Piercing when thrown. Each Scimitar adds 1d6 Cold or 1d6 Fire on a hit, and the Greatsword adds both. It casts Fire Shield twice, regaining uses at dawn, and each attuned creature can cast it only once a day.",{"ch":[2,"2","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Greatsword"],"xd":["+1d6 Cold and +1d6 Fire"]}],["Mageplate Cap","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A pointed hat with chain and metal, for Sorcerers and Wizards. It has 2 charges and regains 1 at dawn. Spend 1 charge to cast Mage Armor on yourself, appearing as plate-like force. Your base AC becomes 15 + Dexterity modifier instead of the normal spell value.",{"by":"Sorcerer or Wizard","ch":[2,"1","dawn"]}],["Magma War Pick","Weapon","Rare",1,"A war pick with +1 to attack and damage rolls and +1d4 Fire damage on a hit. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 at dawn. When you hit a metal target or one in metal armor, spend 1 charge for an extra 2d8 Fire damage.",{"ch":[3,"1d3","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["War Pick"],"xd":["+1d4 Fire"]}],["Mammoth Boots","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Sturdy boots that add 50 lb to your weight without you feeling it. Ice and snow Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement. Forced movement (push, pull, or similar) is reduced by 5 ft.",{}],["Mantle of the Pack Lord","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A pelt cloak that breaks up pack tactics. Enemies do not gain Advantage on attack rolls against you just because an ally of theirs is within 5 ft of you, such as from Pack Tactics.",{}],["Mask of Dendallen","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A skull mask with 5 charges that returns all of them at dusk. Spend 1 charge to cast Bestow Curse, Fear, Speak with Dead or Tongues (save DC 16). You have Advantage on Constitution saves to keep Concentration on those spells and you understand any writing you see.\n**Curse.** On first wearing, make a DC 16 Intelligence save. On a pass you can pull it off at once. On a fail you take 5d10 Psychic damage, cannot remove it without Remove Curse or similar magic, lose smell and taste (you auto-fail Perception checks that need them), and take 1d10 Psychic damage whenever you roll a 1 on a D20 Test. After removal, your face needs 1d4 days to heal and your voice changes.",{"ch":[5,"all","dusk"]}],["Mask of the Pact Bearer","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"The mask takes the face of your patron when you attune. Once per dawn you can cast one spell from your level 3 Warlock subclass spell table without a slot. Its level cannot exceed your Warlock slot level, and it is cast at its lowest level.",{"by":"Warlock","ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Master Machinist's Marvelous Mallet","Weapon","Rare",1,"A mirror-polished silver Light Hammer with +1 to attack and damage rolls. It has 7 charges and regains 1d6 + 1 at dawn. Spend 1 charge to cast Mending from it, affecting an area up to 5 ft on a side. Or spend 3 charges as a Bonus Action and touch armor to give its wearer +1 AC for 1 minute (one such effect per creature).",{"ch":[7,"1d6+1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Light Hammer"]}],["Mastery Gem","Wondrous Item","Legendary",0,"A red gem, immune to all damage, that overrides an attunement requirement you fail. Hold it to an item (not Legendary or an Artifact) and you can attune anyway. The gem fuses to the item, and ending attunement frees you even from a curse. When it detaches it strips the item's magic, leaving it mundane.",{}],["Merry Berry","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A sweet fruit that tastes like shortbread when raw. When cooked properly, the eater has Advantage on Intelligence and Wisdom checks that rely on smell or taste, and on checks with Cook's Utensils, for 24 hours. Overcooking removes the benefit.",{}],["Mirrorlight Edge","Weapon","Rare",1,"A crystal Scimitar. As a Magic action, command it to make up to 2 ghostly projections that last until you dismiss them. When you miss while it has a projection, dismiss one to reroll the d20. When you hit, you deal an extra 1d4 Slashing per projection. It sheds Dim Light in 10 ft with one projection and 20 ft with two.",{"base":["Scimitar"],"xd":["Per projection: +1d4 Slashing"]}],["Mirrorlight Piercer","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A crystal Spear with +2 to attack and damage rolls and the Light property. With a free hand, use a Magic action and a command word to make a ghostly copy in that hand, and make one attack with either. A thrown copy vanishes and then reforms. The copy lasts 1 minute or until you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. The Spear sheds Bright Light in 10 ft and Dim Light for 10 ft more while a copy exists.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Spear"]}],["Mockingblade","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A Shortsword you are proficient with while attuned. It has 6 charges and regains 1d4 + 2 at dawn. When you hit on your turn, spend a Bonus Action and 1 charge to cast Vicious Mockery on the target with your spell save DC. If the target rolls a 20 on the save, the hilt screams at you and the next attack against you has Advantage until your next turn, and the sword cannot cast it again for 1d4 days.",{"by":"Bard","ch":[6,"1d4+2","dawn"],"base":["Shortsword"]}],["Monocle of Clarity","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A lens with three filters and 4 charges, regaining 1d3 + 1 at dawn. As a Magic action, spend 1 charge to activate one filter for up to 1 hour. Comprehend Languages lets you understand any writing you see, Darkvision gives 60 ft, and See Invisibility reveals Invisible creatures and objects.",{"ch":[4,"1d3+1","dawn"]}],["Monsterbane Lasher","Weapon","Very Rare",0,"A mithral Whip with +1 to attack and damage rolls and an extra 1d4 Slashing on a hit. Its seven runes match Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison, Radiant and Thunder. On a melee hit, channel one or more runes to add 2d4 of each chosen type. A rune you channel cannot be used again until dawn.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Whip"],"xd":["Always: +1d4 Slashing","Per rune: +2d4 of its type"]}],["Necrolace","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A necklace that holds up to 3 charges and starts with 1d3. It gains 1 charge when you reduce a Small or larger enemy to 0 HP. As a Bonus Action, spend charges to take 1d8 Necrotic damage each (ignores Resistance and Immunity), and a creature you see within 30 ft regains twice that in HP. If this drops you to 0 HP you are Unconscious but Stable, and the target regains twice your remaining HP instead.",{"by":"Spellcaster","ch":[3,"0","never","Starts with 1d3. Gains 1 per kill"]}],["Nightstalker's Kanabo","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A studded Greatclub with +1 to attack and damage rolls and the Heavy property. It deals an extra 2d8 Psychic damage to an Unconscious target. On a natural 20, the target makes a DC 16 Constitution save or is Unconscious until the end of your next turn (damage or a shake ends it, and creatures that do not sleep or are immune to Exhaustion pass). It has 3 charges, regaining 1d3 at dusk. Spend 1 charge as a Bonus Action to cast Invisibility (self only) or Sleep.",{"ch":[3,"1d3","dusk"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Greatclub"],"xd":["Unconscious target: +2d8 Psychic"]}],["Null Chalk","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"A pouch with 1d4 + 1 chalk sticks. As a Magic action, a stick draws a continuous line up to 50 ft long and 1 ft thick that lasts 8 hours, and the stick crumbles. Magic cannot cross it, creatures behind it have Cover against magic from the far side, and magic items crossing it turn mundane for 1 round. The first Celestial, Elemental, Fey, Fiend or Undead to cross on a turn makes a DC 16 Charisma save. On a fail it takes 2d8 Force damage, is pushed back up to 10 ft and has Speed 0 until its next turn. On a pass it takes half damage and crosses. Dispel Magic treats the line as a level 6 spell.",{}],["Omenbringer's Mantle","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A raven-feathered mantle. You have Resistance to Necrotic damage and fall at 60 ft per round without taking fall damage. You can cast Find Familiar from it as a Magic action, and the familiar is a Raven. If it drops to 0 HP, it cannot be summoned again until dusk.",{"fx":{"res":["Necrotic"]}}],["Orator's Quill","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A red quill that writes what you say. Use a Bonus Action and a command word to activate it, then it floats and writes your words on a still surface, starting a new line at the edge. You must be within 15 ft and it cannot hear you behind Cover. It stops on the command word again or after 1 minute of silence.",{}],["Otyugh Cloak","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"An otyugh pelt with a 3 ft eye tendril on the hood. As a Magic action you can send a simple message or image telepathically to a creature you see within 60 ft that understands a language, with no reply possible. The tendril can do simple tasks within 5 ft (no attacks, no magic items, 10 lb limit). As a Bonus Action with eyes closed, you see through it and gain Darkvision 60 ft.",{}],["Ouroboros Rapier","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Rapier with +1 to attack and damage rolls. Each 8 on a damage die adds 1d8 Poison damage. On a natural 20 against a creature, it makes a DC 15 Constitution save. On a fail it takes 3d6 Poison damage and is Poisoned for 1 minute. On a pass it takes half damage only.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Rapier"],"xd":["Natural 20: DC 15 Con, 3d6 Poison and Poisoned"]}],["Overshield","Armor","Uncommon",1,"A large Shield that gives +1 AC on top of its normal bonus. The bonus is +2 while you have any Temporary HP, and the Shield glows blue. As a Magic action, gain 1d6 + 8 Temporary HP. Once used, it works again at the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"ac":1},"base":["Shield"]}],["Pack of LeviBubble Sugarbombs","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A pack of five gum pieces. Chew one for 1 minute, then as a Magic action blow a bubble 1 ft wide to gain the effect of Levitate (no Concentration) for up to 10 minutes. It ends early if you pop the bubble or it takes damage. You can instead stick the bubble to another creature or loose object within 5 ft. An unwilling target can avoid it with a DC 13 Dexterity save. The gum is mundane afterward.",{}],["Pair of Tiny Violin Rings","Ring","Common",0,"A pair of golden rings that play a sad tune when rubbed together. A creature that knows Vicious Mockery can use them as the Somatic component of that cantrip instead of the Verbal one.",{}],["Pearl of Wisdom Quiver","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A quiver made from a giant oyster shell. Arrows drawn from it are magical, ignore the penalties of underwater ranged combat, and turn mundane once they hit or someone else holds them. Use a command word to make a magical pearl. A creature holding it can take Advantage on one Wisdom check or save, which turns the pearl to dust. An unused pearl fades after 24 hours. Works once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Pendant of the Tempered Fury","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A silvered pendant holding a flaming fist. If you wear no armor and carry no Shield, you reduce Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage you take by 3. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 at dawn. As a Bonus Action, spend 1 charge to wreathe your hands in flame for 1 minute, shedding Bright Light in 10 ft and Dim Light for 10 ft more. Your Unarmed Strike can then deal Fire damage and adds 1d4 Fire on a hit. The flames never harm you.",{"ch":[3,"1d3","dawn"],"xd":["Flaming hands: Unarmed Strike +1d4 Fire"]}],["Pendant of Thieves' Sight","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"You know Thieves' Cant while wearing it. You also gain a +5 bonus to Intelligence checks to understand a written or spoken cipher.",{}],["Peppermince Sugarbomb","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A mint candy that dissolves over 1 hour. As a Bonus Action, crunch it to take 1d6 Piercing damage. For 1 minute, your weapon and Unarmed Strike hits that deal Piercing or Slashing damage deal 2 extra damage. **Upset Stomach.** Only one sugarbomb of this kind works at a time. Eating another while one is active replaces it and forces a DC 13 Constitution save or you are Poisoned for 1 minute.",{}],["Periapt of Reflection","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A mirror-bright charm. When you fail an Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma save, take a Reaction to reroll it and keep the new result.\n**Curse.** Rolling a 1 on such a reroll curses you until Remove Curse or similar magic, even if you take the periapt off. While cursed, the periapt dulls to gray, your reflection within 10 ft looks horrifying, and you take 1d8 Psychic damage whenever you fail an Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma save.",{}],["Permanent Parchment","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A violet sheet that you lock or unlock with a Bonus Action and the words lock or unlock. While locked, it cannot be torn, burned or soaked, and ink on it cannot be changed without magic, and new ink runs off. While unlocked, it acts as plain paper, and the word clear wipes all ink from it.",{}],["Petal Dancer Ward","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A cape of fragrant petals that drift behind you. A Bonus Action changes their color. You can cast Druidcraft from it, and Beasts and Plant creatures have Disadvantage on Opportunity Attacks against you.",{}],["Phase Axe","Weapon","Rare",1,"A near-transparent Battleaxe with +1 to attack and damage rolls and the Thrown property (20/60 ft). The first time on your turn you hit with a ranged attack, another creature within 10 ft of the target makes a DC 15 Dexterity save or takes 1d8 Force damage. If you see the axe within 60 ft, a Bonus Action calls it to your hand, passing through obstacles up to 5 ft thick that are not lead.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Battleaxe"]}],["Pike of the Forgotten Legion","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A Pike with +2 to attack and damage rolls and 6 charges, regaining 1d4 + 2 at dusk. Spend charges to cast Mirror Image (1), Phantom Steed (1), Speak with Dead (1) or Spirit Guardians (2), save DC 17.\n**Spectral Warrior.** Once per turn on a hit, the target has Disadvantage on attacks against you until your next turn. It has no effect on Undead.\n**Haunting Phalanx.** Magic action, 3 charges: spectral pikemen march in a 25 ft wide, 50 ft long Line. Each creature makes a DC 17 Intelligence save (Undead pass), taking 3d10 Necrotic and 3d10 Psychic and the Spectral Warrior effect on a fail, or half damage on a pass.",{"ch":[6,"1d4+2","dusk"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Pike"]}],["Plaguebane Mask","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A bird-beaked mask that purifies airborne toxins. You have Advantage on saves to avoid or end Poisoned and airborne magical contagions, and Resistance to Poison damage from those effects. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 at dawn. As a Magic action, spend 1 charge to exhale a 15 ft Cone of pollen. Each creature makes a DC 15 Constitution save, taking 2d8 Poison and having its Speed halved until the end of its next turn on a fail (not if immune to Poisoned), or half damage only on a pass.",{"ch":[3,"1d3","dawn"]}],["Planar Rapier","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Rapier with +2 to attack and damage rolls and 5 charges, regaining 1d4 + 1 at dawn. When you make a melee attack, spend 1 charge to add 5 ft of reach. Or spend 1 charge after a melee attack on a target within 5 ft to make a second melee attack against a creature 5 ft behind it, which must be within 10 ft of you. Each charge spent adds 2d8 Force damage on a hit.",{"ch":[5,"1d4+1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Rapier"],"xd":["Per charge: +2d8 Force"]}],["Pomade of Ten Thousand Styles","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A canister that changes your hair color, style, thickness and length (up to 1 ft longer or shorter) for 1 minute of application per use. It holds 4 uses and regains 1d4 at dawn. The change fades after a Long Rest unless you repeat it for 7 days, which makes it permanent. Cut hair turns to dust after 24 hours.",{"ch":[4,"1d4","dawn"]}],["Potion of Dragon's Breath","Potion","Unknown",0,"Drinking it gives you 1 minute to replace one attack of the Attack action with a breath like the Dragonborn Breath Weapon. The damage type is rolled on the Draconic Ancestors table at creation. Uncommon is 2d10 with DC 13, Rare is 3d10 with DC 15, Very Rare is 4d10 with DC 16. A potion crafted from a dragon's stomach and gizzard takes that dragon's type, with rarity set by age: young Uncommon, adult Rare, ancient Very Rare. Crafting needs 2 hours of work per day or you roll 1d20, and on a 1 the materials are ruined.",{}],["Potion of Dragon's Breath (Uncommon)","Potion","Uncommon",0,"Drinking it gives you 1 minute to replace one attack of the Attack action with a breath like the Dragonborn Breath Weapon. The damage type is rolled on the Draconic Ancestors table at creation. Uncommon is 2d10 with DC 13, Rare is 3d10 with DC 15, Very Rare is 4d10 with DC 16. A potion crafted from a dragon's stomach and gizzard takes that dragon's type, with rarity set by age: young Uncommon, adult Rare, ancient Very Rare. Crafting needs 2 hours of work per day or you roll 1d20, and on a 1 the materials are ruined.",{}],["Potion of Dragon's Breath (Rare)","Potion","Rare",0,"Drinking it gives you 1 minute to replace one attack of the Attack action with a breath like the Dragonborn Breath Weapon. The damage type is rolled on the Draconic Ancestors table at creation. Uncommon is 2d10 with DC 13, Rare is 3d10 with DC 15, Very Rare is 4d10 with DC 16. A potion crafted from a dragon's stomach and gizzard takes that dragon's type, with rarity set by age: young Uncommon, adult Rare, ancient Very Rare. Crafting needs 2 hours of work per day or you roll 1d20, and on a 1 the materials are ruined.",{}],["Potion of Dragon's Breath (Very Rare)","Potion","Very Rare",0,"Drinking it gives you 1 minute to replace one attack of the Attack action with a breath like the Dragonborn Breath Weapon. The damage type is rolled on the Draconic Ancestors table at creation. Uncommon is 2d10 with DC 13, Rare is 3d10 with DC 15, Very Rare is 4d10 with DC 16. A potion crafted from a dragon's stomach and gizzard takes that dragon's type, with rarity set by age: young Uncommon, adult Rare, ancient Very Rare. Crafting needs 2 hours of work per day or you roll 1d20, and on a 1 the materials are ruined.",{}],["Potion of Spell Recovery","Potion","Rare",0,"Drinking it restores expended spell slots of your choice, each of level 1 to 5, with a combined level of 1d3 + 3 or less.",{}],["Precipit, the Formless","Staff","Artifact",1,"A coral staff from the Plane of Water that works as a Quarterstaff (Topple). Attuned, you breathe underwater, ignore deep-water drawbacks and have Resistance to Cold damage. It has 15 charges and regains 1d8 + 7 at dawn. As a Bonus Action, set it to gas, liquid or solid, or spend 1 charge as a Reaction to change at once.\n**Gas.** Resist Bludgeoning and Piercing, +10 ft Speed, Fly Speed equal to your Speed, move through creatures, and Disadvantage on Opportunity Attacks against you. Spells (DC 18): Cloudkill 5, Fog Cloud 1, Gaseous Form 3, Misty Step 2, Wind Walk 6. Tailwind (2 charges): you and allies within 30 ft Dash as a Bonus Action and avoid Opportunity Attacks until the end of your next turn.\n**Liquid.** Resist Bludgeoning and Slashing, +10 ft Speed, Swim Speed equal to your Speed, walk on liquid, and redirect a melee miss against you. Spells (DC 18): Blur 2, Control Water 4, Create or Destroy Water 1, Mirror Image 2, Water Breathing 3. Tide Turner (3 charges): enemies within 30 ft make a DC 18 Strength save, taking 4d8 Bludgeoning and a 20 ft push or pull on a fail, or half damage on a pass.\n**Solid.** Resist Piercing and Slashing, Speed 5 ft, +3 AC, halved forced movement, and 10 Temporary HP at the start of each turn. Spells (DC 18, +10 to hit): Cone of Cold 5, Ice Storm 4, Ray of Frost 0 (1 at level 5), Wall of Ice 6. Deep Freeze (4 charges): enemies within 30 ft make a DC 18 Constitution save, taking 4d8 Cold and Speed 0 until the end of their next turn on a fail, or half damage and half Speed on a pass.\nIt can only be destroyed by 100 years without water on the Plane of Water.",{"ch":[15,"1d8+7","dawn"],"fx":{"res":["Cold"]},"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Prismatic Javelin","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A dark crystal Javelin that returns to your hand after a ranged hit. Once per dawn, throw it at a point within 120 ft as a Magic action to burst into Bright Light in 20 ft and Dim Light for 20 ft more. Each creature of your choice there not behind Cover makes a DC 13 Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 2d10 damage from a beam rolled on 1d6: 1 Red Fire, 2 Orange Acid, 3 Yellow Lightning, 4 Green Poison, 5 Blue Cold, 6 hit by two beams (reroll any 6).",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"base":["Javelin"]}],["Profane Mask","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A cloth mask that turns your spoken words into angry insults and swears, which you do not hear. A Study action and a DC 10 Intelligence (Investigation) check shows the words are not yours. Verbal components, command words and actual obscenities are heard normally.",{}],["Purging Dagger","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A holy wood Dagger with +1 to attack and damage rolls and an extra 1d4 Radiant on a hit, rising to 2d4 against Undead. On a natural 20 against an Undead, you can leave it lodged in the target. It then sheds sunlight (Bright 15 ft, Dim 15 ft more) and deals 3d4 Radiant at the start of the target's turns. Pulling it out takes an action and a DC 16 Strength (Athletics) check, and it then returns to the ground at your feet or your free hand.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Dagger"],"xd":["Always: +1d4 Radiant","Undead: +2d4 Radiant instead"]}],["Purity Spear","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A unicorn-horn Spear with +2 to attack and damage rolls. Attuned, you are immune to Poison damage and Poisoned, and have Advantage on Constitution and Wisdom saves against spells and magical effects. It has 10 charges, regaining 1d6 + 4 at dawn. Spend charges to cast Calm Emotions 2, Detect Evil and Good 1, Dispel Evil and Good 5, Greater Restoration 5, Misty Step 2 or Purify Food and Drink 1 (DC 17). As a Magic action, spend 1 charge to heal a touched creature 2d8 + 2 HP and end Poisoned on it.\n**Charge.** Moving 20 ft straight at a target before a melee hit adds 2d8 Piercing.\n**Curse Breaker.** You cannot be cursed, and existing curses on you are suppressed while attuned.",{"by":"Creature of Good Alignment","ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2,"imm":["Poison"],"condImm":["Poisoned"]},"base":["Spear"],"xd":["Moved 20 ft straight: +2d8 Piercing"]}],["Purse Piglet","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A ceramic piggy bank that animates once you drop in a coin and cork it, and treats you as its owner. It eats coins (up to 1,000 per hour), tells you its total when shaken, and spits out exact change on request, even converting denominations. It keeps at least 1 Copper Piece unless you remove it. It follows you or a designated ally, vanishes into a pocket dimension if none is within 30 ft, and is summoned or sent away with a Bonus Action and its command phrase.\nIt is a Tiny object with AC 10 and 5 HP, immune to Poison and Psychic, and vulnerable to Bludgeoning. At 0 HP it shatters and returns after 1d4 days. Putting it in a Bag of Holding, Portable Hole or similar space destroys both and opens an Astral Plane gate that pulls in creatures within 10 ft.",{}],["Puzzle Ring of Vitality, Life, and Power","Ring","Legendary",1,"A golden ring with a silver puzzle ring of three bands. You can use Lay On Hands on a creature up to 10 ft away. As a Study action, solve one band at a time in order. Band one is DC 5 Intelligence (Investigation) and starts a 30 ft Emanation for 1 minute that restores 2d6 HP to one creature in it at creation and the start of each of your turns. Band two is DC 10 and gives you and allies Resistance to Necrotic, protects HP maximums, and brings an ally at 0 HP to 1 HP at the start of its turn. Band three is DC 15 and gives you and allies Advantage on saves against spells and magical effects, and no damage on a successful half-damage save. The aura ends if you remove the ring or drop to 0 HP, and then the ring waits 1 day per band solved. If you solved all three, roll 1d3, and on a 1 or 2 reduce the wait by that number, on a 3 it is ready at once.",{"by":"Paladin"}],["Quagmire Maul","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A damp, withered Maul with +2 to attack and damage rolls and 10 charges, regaining 1d6 + 4 at dawn. As a Magic action, spend 1 or more charges and slam it down within 5 ft to turn a 5 ft radius into a swamp of Difficult Terrain for 1 minute, plus 5 ft radius per extra charge. You cross it as normal terrain. If you spend the last charge, roll 1d20, and on a 1 the maul turns to muck and is destroyed.",{"ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Maul"]}],["Quake Hammer","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Light Hammer with +2 to attack and damage rolls. Once per dawn, as a Magic action, smash it down within 5 ft or throw it at a point within 60 ft to shake a 10 ft radius. Each creature there except you makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking 2d6 Bludgeoning and falling Prone on a fail, or half damage only on a pass.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Light Hammer"]}],["Quickdraw","Weapon","Rare",0,"A concealed Hand Crossbow worn on the wrist or forearm that needs no free hand. You must also wear two rings on adjacent fingers, one with a string and one with a tiny blade. Severing the string fires it. Reloading and resetting takes 1 minute. While loaded, you can attack with it as a Bonus Action, or as a Reaction at the start of your first turn of combat.",{"base":["Hand Crossbow"]}],["Quicksilver Clay","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A 1-inch orb of dry, silvery liquid. As a Magic action, shape it into any form no larger than your palm. It stays liquid, reverts at will with no action, and reverts at once if it leaves your hand. Swallowing it is harmless and it passes in 1d4 days.",{}],["Radiant Defender","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Maul with a guard shield over the handle and +1 to attack and damage rolls. When you take the Dodge action while wielding it, you gain +2 AC until your next turn. If a creature within 5 ft misses you while you benefit from Dodge, use a Reaction to attack it with the Maul, adding 1d8 Radiant on a hit. Using that Reaction ends the AC bonus until you Dodge again.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Maul"],"xd":["Reaction hit: +1d8 Radiant"]}],["Reap and Sew","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Light Crossbow with +2 to attack and damage rolls that deals Force damage. You can cast Mending from it. Its special needle Bolt returns and reloads itself after each attack, so you ignore Loading. It has 4 charges and regains 1d4 at dawn. When you hit a Large or smaller creature with that Bolt, spend 1 charge to tether it to a point within 5 ft of it. If it moves more than 10 ft away before the end of its next turn, it makes a DC 15 Strength save or has Speed 0 until your next turn. A lost Bolt returns after 24 hours.\n**Curse.** Attuning curses you. Each time you start a Short or Long Rest you make a DC 12 Wisdom save, and on a fail you must sew or knit feverishly for at least 1 hour first.",{"ch":[4,"1d4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Light Crossbow"]}],["Red Claw's Regalia","Wondrous Item","Legendary",1,"A dragon scale robe that is warm and comfortable. You tolerate temperatures of 0 degrees F or lower, your Constitution rises by 2 (maximum 22), you have Advantage on Constitution saves and Resistance to Fire damage, and you can walk on molten rock as if solid. Harmless embers and scorch marks trail your steps.",{"fx":{"res":["Fire"]}}],["Relentless Bulwark","Armor","Uncommon",1,"A sturdy metal Shield with 6 charges, regaining 1d4 + 2 at dawn. Spend 1 charge to cast Shield of Faith from it. If you fail a Constitution save to hold that Concentration, you can spend another charge as a Reaction to pass instead, while holding the Shield.",{"by":"Cleric or Paladin","ch":[6,"1d4+2","dawn"],"base":["Shield"]}],["Retaliating Bloom Shield","Armor","Rare",0,"A steel Shield with a hidden chamber of toxic pollen. While holding it, when a Large or smaller creature you see within 5 ft misses you, use a Reaction to blast it. It makes a DC 15 Constitution save, taking 3d10 Poison and becoming Poisoned for 1 minute on a fail, or half damage on a pass. Works again at the next dusk, or you can reset the plates by hand over 1 minute.",{"ch":[1,"1","dusk"],"base":["Shield"]}],["Retaliating Shield of Ink","Armor","Uncommon",0,"A Shield that sprays squid ink. When a Large or smaller creature within 5 ft misses you, use a Reaction to spray it. The attacker makes a Dexterity save or is Blinded until the start of its next turn. The DC is 13 with squid ink (20+ gp) or 10 with common ink (10 gp). It holds 3 uses and takes 1 minute to refill. A Study action and DC 12 Intelligence (Investigation) check reveals how it works. Filling it with acid, poison, grog, oil or sand damages it and takes 8 hours to repair.",{"ch":[3,"0","never","Refill takes 1 minute"],"base":["Shield"]}],["Ring of Anchoring","Ring","Rare",1,"A lead ring that lets you breathe underwater and cuts any forced movement against you by 10 ft.\n**Curse.** Attuning curses you until Remove Curse or similar magic, or until the ring finger is severed. You cannot remove it, and underwater the ring arm is so heavy you have Disadvantage on Strength and Dexterity checks. Whenever you become submerged, make a DC 20 Strength save. On a fail the arm is immobile for 1 minute, your Speed is 0, and you are dragged 30 ft down at the start of each turn. On a pass your Speed is halved and you have Disadvantage on attacks with that arm. Repeat the save each minute you stay submerged.",{}],["Ring of Eldritch Ire","Ring","Rare",1,"A warped ring with three swiveling gems. It has 3 charges and regains all at dusk. As a Bonus Action, spend 1 charge to mark a creature you see within 60 ft for 1 hour. You gain +1 to attack and damage rolls against it, it has -1 on saves against your spells, you know its distance and direction on the same plane, and within 60 ft you perceive it as if with Truesight, seeing through visual illusions.",{"by":"Warlock","ch":[3,"all","dusk"]}],["Ring of Fire","Ring","Rare",0,"Cast Wall of Fire from the ring (save DC 15). It appears as a stationary 10 ft Emanation around you, 20 ft high and 1 ft thick. Once used, it works again at the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Ring of Gestures","Ring","Common",0,"A gaudy ring with a pink gem shaped like a hand. You can cast Minor Illusion from it to change how that hand looks, such as making fingers bigger, smaller or another color. The gem copies each gesture you make with that hand.",{}],["Ring of Ice","Ring","Very Rare",0,"Cast Wall of Ice from the ring (save DC 16). It appears as a stationary 10 ft Emanation around you, 10 ft high and 1 ft thick. Once used, it works again at the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Ring of Roses","Ring","Common",0,"As a Magic action, a rose grows in your hand. It has a 1 ft stem with small dull thorns, no scent and a color you choose, and it turns to dust after 24 hours.",{}],["Ring of Seething","Ring","Uncommon",1,"When you attune, choose Aberration, Celestial, Dragon, Elemental, Fey, Fiend or Undead. The band glows red hot when a creature of that type is within 60 ft, though it only feels faintly warm to you. You have Advantage on saves against being Charmed or Frightened by that type.\n**Curse.** Attuning curses you until Remove Curse or similar magic. You cannot remove the ring, have Disadvantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Charisma checks involving that type, and while one is within 60 ft you have Disadvantage on attacks against creatures of other types.",{}],["Ring of Stone","Ring","Rare",0,"Cast Wall of Stone from the ring (save DC 16). It appears as a stationary 10 ft Emanation around you, 10 ft high and 6 inches thick. Once used, it works again at the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Ring of the Fowl Sentinel","Ring","Common",0,"A bronze ring stamped with a rooster. As a Magic action, tap it to the beak of a chicken or rooster that is not Hostile to make it Charmed for 8 hours. It then has AC 10, 1 HP, Speed 0, +3 to Wisdom (Perception) and stays quiet. If it sees a new Small or larger creature, or the charm ends, it crows loudly, heard out to 150 ft. Tapping it again ends the charm without a cry. Only one creature can be charmed this way at a time.",{}],["Ring of the Sandskimmer","Ring","Uncommon",0,"A ring of flowing sand around a spinning tiger's eye stone. You leave no footprints in sand, and sand-based Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement.",{}],["Ring of Wind","Ring","Uncommon",0,"Cast Wind Wall from the ring (save DC 13). It appears as a stationary 10 ft Emanation around you, 15 ft high and 1 ft thick. Once used, it works again at the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Rocborne Hand Ballista","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A massive Heavy Crossbow with +1 to attack and damage rolls and twin handles. It uses twice the normal ammunition, deals an extra 1d10 Piercing on a hit, and screeches audibly out to 100 ft when fired. It has 5 charges and regains 1d4 + 1 at dawn. When you hit a Huge or smaller creature with a ranged attack, spend 1 charge. It makes a DC 16 Constitution save or has Speed 0 and cannot make Opportunity Attacks until the start of your next turn.",{"ch":[5,"1d4+1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Heavy Crossbow"],"xd":["Always: +1d10 Piercing"]}],["Rocborne Robe","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A warm canvas robe lined with roc down that lets you tolerate temperatures of 0 degrees F or lower. It has 5 charges and regains 1d4 + 1 at dawn. As a Magic action, spend 1 charge to flap wings that blast a 15 ft wide, 10 ft long Line of wind. Each Medium or smaller creature there makes a DC 13 Strength save or is pushed 10 ft away. You are flung 10 ft backward without provoking Opportunity Attacks.",{"ch":[5,"1d4+1","dawn"]}],["Rocborne Rod","Rod","Rare",1,"A rod carved with five rocs and holding 5 charges, regaining 1d4 + 1 at dawn. Spend 1 charge, as a Reaction while falling or a Magic action otherwise, to grow wings that slow your fall to 10 ft per round (20 ft if you weigh over 200 lb). You can move as if you had a 40 ft Fly Speed but not upward, and you take no fall damage. Spend 1 charge as a Magic action to blast a 20 ft radius, 60 ft high Cylinder near you. Large and smaller creatures make a DC 15 Strength save or are launched 30 ft up, as are loose objects under 200 lb. You can choose to fail, and if you also call the wings you launch 60 ft.",{"ch":[5,"1d4+1","dawn"]}],["Sandstorm Dancer","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A golden cloak that billows illusory sand. It has 8 charges and regains 1d6 + 2 at dawn. Spend charges to cast Blur (2), Call Lightning (3), Create or Destroy Water (1) or Hallucinatory Terrain (4), save DC 15.",{"ch":[8,"1d6+2","dawn"]}],["Scholar's Cap +1","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A hat holding the knowledge of past scholars. You gain +1 to Intelligence checks and Intelligence saving throws. For every 5 days of research on a subject, you gain 1 extra day of knowledge.",{}],["Scholar's Cap +2","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A hat holding the knowledge of past scholars. You gain +2 to Intelligence checks and Intelligence saving throws. For every 5 days of research on a subject, you gain 2 extra days of knowledge.",{}],["Scholar's Cap +3","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A hat holding the knowledge of past scholars. You gain +3 to Intelligence checks and Intelligence saving throws. For every 5 days of research on a subject, you gain 3 extra days of knowledge.",{}],["Scorching Cleaver","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Battleaxe with +1 to attack and damage rolls and 8 charges, regaining 1d6 + 2 at dawn. While it has at least 1 charge, hits deal an extra 1d6 Fire. A natural 20 on an attack restores 3 charges.\n**Erupting Slash.** Magic action, spend 3 or more charges: a 5 ft wide, 30 ft long Line of fire. Creatures in it make a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + charges spent) or take 1d6 Fire per charge spent. If you spend 4 or more and leave it at 0 charges, it overheats for an extra 3d6 Fire, and a successful save halves the damage.",{"ch":[8,"1d6+2","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Battleaxe"],"xd":["Has charges: +1d6 Fire"]}],["Screaming Longbow","Weapon","Rare",1,"A sickly Longbow whose arrows howl audibly out to 100 ft. A hit deals an extra 2d4 Thunder. On a natural 20, the target and each creature within 5 ft of it make a DC 15 Constitution save or are Deafened for 1 minute.",{"base":["Longbow"],"xd":["Always: +2d4 Thunder"]}],["Sea Serpent Hairpin","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A golden hairpin coiled around a tiny silver sword. When you grapple with Unarmed Strike while submerged or swimming, the target has Disadvantage on checks and saves to avoid or end the Grappled condition.",{}],["Seafarer's Jacket","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A captain's jacket that sheds water. You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed and proficiency with Navigator's Tools (Expertise if you already had it). Once per dawn you can cast Fog Cloud from it at level 2.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Seat Belt","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A belt you wear while standing on solid ground. As you begin to sit, spend a Bonus Action to summon an Invisible, incorporeal chair of any style that holds up to 500 lb. You cannot do anything with it except sit. It vanishes if the ground is no longer solid or you stand up.",{}],["Seed of Rebirth","Wondrous Item","Legendary",1,"A fist-sized seed that up to 4 creatures can attune to during a Long Rest. If each plants it together in fertile soil, it grows in 7 days into a 60 ft tree with a 30 ft Emanation canopy and one large limb per attuned creature. Once planted, no one else can attune, and attunement survives distance and death. Attunement ends if a creature commits a malicious affront to nature.\nWhen an attuned creature has been dead for 1 minute, its soul goes to the tree and its body becomes rich soil like the Plant Growth enrichment. After 1d6 + 1 days a nut falls and reveals the creature in a new body, as Reincarnate, ending its attunement. A limb dies as each attunement ends. The tree cannot be destroyed by nonmagical means, and attuned creatures sense attacks on it. When the last limb dies, the tree splits and releases another seed to a new plane.",{}],["Septum Ring of the Great Minotaur","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A tempered gold nose ring set with rubies. Your Strength rises by 2 (maximum 22) and you have Advantage on Strength checks. Your carrying capacity doubles and you perfectly recall any path you traveled in the last 24 hours.",{}],["Serpent Dart","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Dart you can coat with emerald poison as a Bonus Action. The poison lasts 1 minute or until it hits a creature, which makes a DC 13 Constitution save or takes an extra 2d8 Poison and is Poisoned for 1 minute. Once used, it works again at the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"base":["Dart"]}],["Servitude Choker","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A necklace that animates a small object. As a Magic action, wrap it around a Small or smaller nonmagical object under 50 lb that is not attached or carried. It becomes a mindless servant under your control (AC 10, Speed 20 ft) until you remove the necklace or it takes damage. Command it with a Bonus Action within 60 ft. It does simple chores but cannot attack, activate magic items or carry over 10 lb. It lasts up to 8 hours, then the choker cannot be used for 1d8 hours.",{}],["Set of Numat's Trick Tubes","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Two linked ceramic tubes, each 3 inches wide and 1 ft tall. Close an object inside one and it teleports to the other, up to 2 lb at a time and never a creature. Both tubes must be on the same plane with their lids closed.",{}],["Set of Secret Scribe Candles","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Two linked candles that never run out and never ignite Paper or Parchment. Light one while the other is unlit and it burns blue. Held under a page, the blue flame burns off nonmagical ink. When you put it out, the other candle lights with an orange lavender flame that only magic can put out. Under a blank page, it burns the first page's ink onto it over 1 minute, then goes out.",{}],["Shadow Drinker","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Dagger with +1 to attack and damage rolls. When you hit a Small or larger enemy in melee, you can absorb its shadow. It then casts no shadow, and dark haze wraps you and the blade for up to 10 minutes. In the haze you are Invisible while entirely in Dim Light or Darkness. Hits deal an extra 1d6 Psychic, or 2d6 against the shadowless creature. The haze ends after you attack, deal damage or cast a spell, or as a Bonus Action, and the shadow returns. You can hold one shadow at a time, and the same creature's shadow cannot be taken again until dusk.\n**Curse.** Attuning curses you until Remove Curse or similar magic. While cursed, you have Vulnerability to Radiant damage.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Dagger"],"xd":["Shadow haze: +1d6 Psychic (2d6 vs shadowless)"]}],["Shadow Ink","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A bottle of ink that can only be seen and read in total darkness, where writing, drawings and tattoos glow with soft colored light. One bottle fills 50 pages. Detect Magic reveals only a faint trace of magic.",{}],["Shadow Ward","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A still cloak that drinks in light. You have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 at dusk. When you are hit by an attack, take a Reaction and spend 1 charge to halve the damage (round down) and teleport in black smoke to an unoccupied space you see within 30 ft.",{"ch":[3,"1d3","dusk"]}],["Shadowshawl","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A shawl of thick fabric that looks like spider webs. With the hood up, your face sits in a pocket of magical Darkness and you gain Darkvision 60 ft, or +60 ft if you already have it. You see through the pocket normally, and light-based effects such as Sunbeam cannot Blind you.",{"fx":{"dark":60}}],["Shadowsmoke Dragon Pipe","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A pipe with 4 charges, regaining 1d3 + 1 at dawn, that leaves odorless smoke. As a Magic action, spend 1 charge to blow a smoke ring at yourself or an ally you see within 30 ft. The target can turn Invisible at once or wear the ring (one at a time, for 1 minute) and turn Invisible later with a Bonus Action. The Invisible condition lasts until the start of its next turn or until it attacks, deals damage or casts a spell.",{"ch":[4,"1d3+1","dawn"]}],["Shaedenstaff","Staff","Very Rare",1,"A staff from the horn of a huge Undead. It works as a Quarterstaff (Topple), and attuned you have Advantage on saves against mental stress effects. It has 15 charges and regains 2d6 + 3 at dusk. If you spend the last, roll 1d20, and on a 1 it crumbles in black smoke with a scream heard out to 300 ft.\n**Annihilating Strike.** On a melee hit, spend 1 charge for an extra 1d10 Necrotic.\n**Spells.** Using your save DC, spend charges for Calm Emotions 1, Darkness 2, Inflict Wounds 3 (level 3), Dispel Evil and Good 5 or Circle of Death 6.",{"by":"Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard","ch":[15,"2d6+3","dusk"],"base":["Quarterstaff"],"xd":["Spend 1 charge: +1d10 Necrotic"]}],["Shape-Shifter's Circlet","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Spend 1 minute massaging your ears, forehead or temples to copy one cosmetic feature of another creature. Pick one: other ears, horns or antlers on your head, or different eyes (color and pupil shape). Only one effect at a time. It ends when you dismiss it as a Bonus Action, remove the circlet or fall Unconscious. You gain no senses or abilities from the copied feature.",{}],["Shared Burden","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"Chained rings and bracers that symbolize a Warlock's pact. They count as a Spellcasting Focus for your Warlock spells. When a Warlock spell damages a creature, you can add your Charisma modifier (min 1) to the damage. If you do, you take Psychic damage equal to half your Charisma modifier (round up), which ignores Resistance and Immunity.",{"by":"a Warlock"}],["Sharkrazor Mantle","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A sharkskin cloak that gives you a Swim Speed of 60 ft and lets you breathe underwater. A creature that grapples or Restrains you while touching you takes 1d6 Piercing damage, and again at the start of each of its turns until the condition ends or it stops touching you. You have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception or Survival) checks to find or track a creature missing Hit Points. Your attacks against an Invisible target missing Hit Points do not suffer Disadvantage from that condition.",{"fx":{"swim":60}}],["Sheer Cold","Weapon","Rare",0,"A Battleaxe with a blade of Everglacier ice. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls, and it deals Cold damage instead of Slashing. On a roll of 20 on the attack, choose a 15 ft Cone or a 30 ft long, 5 ft wide Line toward the target. It turns to slick ice for 1 minute and counts as Difficult Terrain. A creature entering it for the first time on a turn or starting its turn there makes a DC 10 Dexterity save or falls Prone. The original target also makes a DC 15 Dexterity save or is Restrained until the start of your next turn, and it can end that with an action and a DC 15 Strength check.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Battleaxe"]}],["Shield of Yggdrasil","Armor","Very Rare",1,"A massive dwarven tower Shield that needs Strength 17 to wield. It gives +1 AC on top of a normal Shield. **Shield Plant.** As a Bonus Action, plant it in your space for Cover against ranged attacks from your facing. While planted, your Speed is 5 ft and cannot rise, and you reduce Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage from weapons and Unarmed Strikes by 3. Uproot it as a Utilize action. Doffing it while planting (Magic action) leaves it standing as Cover for others. It falls if you are Unconscious or if a creature within 5 ft knocks it over with a DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check. It has 3 charges and regains all at dawn. Spend 1 charge when planting it, or later as a Bonus Action, to spread metal roots in a 10 ft Emanation that is Difficult Terrain for others but not for you and your allies.",{"ch":[3,"all","dawn"],"fx":{"ac":3},"base":["Shield"]}],["Shielding Turtle Sugarbombs","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A pack of two chocolate candies. As a Magic action, eat one to lower your Speed by 10 ft for 1 minute. If you are trained with Shields and carry one on your back, you gain +1 AC for that time. You get no AC bonus if you wield a Shield. **Upset Stomach.** Only one sugarbomb with this property can be active. Eating another ends the first and forces a DC 13 Constitution save, and on a failure you are Poisoned for 1 minute.",{}],["Signet Rings of Blindness, Deafness, and Silence","Ring","Rare",0,"Three skull signets, one each for eyes, ears and mouth. Each ring has 1 charge and regains it at dawn. While wearing the matching ring, you can spend its charge (no action) to end the Blinded or Deafened condition, or to speak a word through magical silence. Worn together, the rings pool their charges so one ring's power can be used several times.",{"ch":[3,"3","dawn"]}],["Signet Rings of the Fey Court","Ring","Very Rare",1,"Four wooden rings, one per season. You must wear all four to attune. You know Druidcraft and gain Elf's Trance if you lack it. Each ring has 2 charges and regains all on a Long Rest. **Season's Resistance.** As a Reaction when you take the matching damage, spend 1 charge for Resistance to it until your next turn starts, including against the triggering hit. Spring is Radiant, summer Fire, autumn Necrotic, winter Cold. **Magic Resistance.** As a Reaction when an enemy targets you with a spell or magical effect, spend any 2 charges to have Advantage on saves against spells and magical effects until your next turn starts.",{"by":"an Elf or Fey creature","ch":[8,"all","long"]}],["Silken Socks of Slickening","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Wear both iridescent socks to cast Grease (save DC 13) centered on a point within 5 ft of you. It works once, then again after the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Silver Eagle Weapon","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A silvered elven Greataxe, Greatsword, Maul or Musket. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls, and it deals 2d6 damage on a hit instead of its normal dice. A Critical Hit does not double the dice. Instead, when both damage dice show the same number, roll 1d6 and add it. Keep rolling extra dice while each new roll matches the one before.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1}}],["Silver Lycan Chime","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A small silver bell steeped in Divination magic, strongest under a full moon. When hung, it rings a melody if a Lycanthrope passes within 15 ft, or within 60 ft during a full moon. It is quiet but audible out to 100 ft, and each kind of Lycanthrope has its own melody.",{}],["Singing Stein","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A pewter stein with a face that sings when it holds at least a sip of potable alcohol. The song fits the drink: wine gives a ballad, rum a sea shanty, ale a drinking song. Mixed drinks make it alternate or blend lyrics. Several steins with the same drink sing in harmony. Poisoned drink makes it sing slightly off key, and a Search action with a successful Wisdom (Perception) check (DC set by the GM) notices it.",{}],["Sirensong Silencer","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A golden ear cuff you put on as a Magic action. You have Advantage on saves to avoid or end the Charmed condition. Tapping it twice (no action) makes you Deafened, though you still faintly hear the sea. Tapping twice again ends it.",{}],["Sling of the Tiny Giant","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Sling that is deadly against larger foes. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. A ranged hit deals an extra 1d4 Force damage per size category the target is larger than you, up to 3d4. On a roll of 20 on the attack, the target makes a DC 15 Strength save or is pushed 10 ft away and knocked Prone. A Large or larger target has Disadvantage on that save.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Sling"]}],["Smash Potatoes","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Fist-shaped potatoes grown by war clerics. Eating one makes your hands itch for 1 hour. For that time, your Unarmed Strike with a hand can deal 1d4 instead of its normal damage. Each extra potato adds 1 hour. You can eat up to three before a Long Rest.",{}],["Snuff","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A dark Sickle with a harsh angle and power over light. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls, and it deals an extra 1d6 Psychic damage. As a Magic action with a command word, extinguish all nonmagical flames within 60 ft and dispel spell-made Bright or Dim Light within 60 ft as Dispel Magic (+4 modifier). Once used, it needs the next dusk. As a Magic action, extend the handle into a scythe wreathed in shadow with the Two-Handed and Reach properties and extra Psychic damage of 2d6. A Bonus Action returns it to Sickle form.",{"ch":[1,"1","dusk"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Sickle"]}],["Snugglebeast (Dragon)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"An enchanted toy. A creature that spends a Short Rest snuggling it and also spends Hit Point Dice at the end of that rest regains an extra 3d6 Hit Points. Only one Snugglebeast helps a creature at a time. After use, that creature cannot benefit from the same toy until it finishes a Long Rest.",{}],["Snugglebeast (Owlbear)","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"An enchanted toy. A creature that spends a Short Rest snuggling it and also spends Hit Point Dice at the end of that rest regains an extra 1d6 Hit Points. Only one Snugglebeast helps a creature at a time. After use, that creature cannot benefit from the same toy until it finishes a Long Rest.",{}],["Snugglebeast (Tarrasque)","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"An enchanted toy. A creature that spends a Short Rest snuggling it and also spends Hit Point Dice at the end of that rest regains an extra 4d6 Hit Points. Only one Snugglebeast helps a creature at a time. After use, that creature cannot benefit from the same toy until it finishes a Long Rest.",{}],["Snugglebeast (Unicorn)","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"An enchanted toy. A creature that spends a Short Rest snuggling it and also spends Hit Point Dice at the end of that rest regains an extra 2d6 Hit Points. Only one Snugglebeast helps a creature at a time. After use, that creature cannot benefit from the same toy until it finishes a Long Rest.",{}],["Snugglebeasts","Wondrous Item","Unknown",0,"A family of enchanted toys in four forms: Owlbear (Common, extra 1d6 Hit Points), Unicorn (Uncommon, 2d6), Dragon (Rare, 3d6) and Tarrasque (Very Rare, 4d6). See each entry for the rules.",{}],["Socks of the Well-Rested","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Wear both socks when you finish a Long Rest to gain Temporary Hit Points equal to 1d8 plus your Constitution modifier.",{}],["Spellwoven Robe","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A robe of magic-sensitive thread that shows glyphs when you cast. While you wear it and no armor, your base AC is 10 plus your spellcasting ability modifier. When you cast a level 1+ spell in it, you can change its look, color and material. It stays a robe of the same weight.",{}],["Spiderbite Daggers","Weapon","Rare",0,"A pair of Daggers made from the fangs of a large venomous spider. When you hit the same creature with both on your turn, it makes a DC 13 Constitution save or takes an extra 2d4 Poison damage and is Poisoned until the end of its next turn.",{"base":["Dagger"]}],["Spire Seed","Wondrous Item","Legendary",1,"A 1 ft long seed in a protective cone. Plant it while attuned and it becomes a 300 ft tall, 40 ft wide tree in 30 days. Only you can then attune to it, and your attunement survives distance and your death (for up to 1 minute dead) but ends if you are on another plane for 24 hours. If it ends before the tree is grown, the tree dies. A loyal Dryad guards the door with the key stem, and once she opens it the tree is yours. Inside are ten floors you lay out, hidden from Divination and teleportation. The tree has AC 20, HP 500, Immunity to Poison, Psychic and nonmagical weapon damage (except siege equipment) and Resistance to the rest. The door has AC 15, HP 100. The tree regains 1d6 HP at dawn, and lost parts regrow in 7 days. If attacked, it calls a Treant once per day until dawn. Neither creature strays over 1 mile. If the dryad is killed, the tree loses its magic. It makes a new Spire Seed every 100 years.",{}],["Spirit Pike","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Pike that you can use with proficiency even if you lack it. When you cast Spiritual Weapon while holding it, the Pike can dissolve and become the spectral weapon. Its hit deals Force damage of 1d10 plus your spellcasting modifier, and the spell's higher-slot scaling stays 1d8 per level. The Pike returns when the spell ends. It has 4 charges and regains all at dawn. When you hit with it, in either form, spend 1 charge for an extra 1d8 Radiant damage.",{"by":"a Cleric","ch":[4,"all","dawn"],"base":["Pike"]}],["Splintershot","Weapon","Rare",0,"A Shortbow that shatters an Arrow into magical shrapnel. As a Magic action with a command word, destroy one nonmagical nocked Arrow. Each creature in a 15 ft Cone makes a DC 15 Dexterity save and takes 2d6 Piercing damage on a failure, or 3d6 if within 5 ft of you.",{"base":["Shortbow"]}],["Splitter","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Halberd with a hatchet-like blade. While holding it with two hands, use a Bonus Action and a command word to split it into a Handaxe and a Quarterstaff, each with the Light property. Repeat to rejoin them. You gain +3 to attack and damage rolls with the Halberd, or +1 with each part when split. **Halberd.** When you roll a 10 on the damage die, the target's Speed drops by 10 ft until your next turn starts and yours rises by 10 ft. **Handaxe and Quarterstaff.** Wielded in separate hands, you gain +1 AC and add your ability modifier to the Light-property bonus attack if it is not already added. The Quarterstaff deals Necrotic damage and maximum damage to plants. The Handaxe returns to your hand right after a ranged attack.",{"fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3,"ac":1},"base":["Halberd"]}],["Squasher","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A big, tough squash that works as a magic weapon. A Druid wielding it can use Wisdom instead of Strength for its melee attack and damage rolls.",{"base":["Greatclub"]}],["Staff of Favorable Winds","Staff","Very Rare",1,"Wind-caused Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement. The staff has 10 charges and regains 1d6 + 4 at dawn. Spend charges to cast, using your spell save DC: Cone of Cold (5), Feather Fall (1), Gust of Wind (2) or Wind Wall (3). As a Magic action, create a harmless sensory effect with air, such as rustling leaves or billowing clothes. If you spend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff turns to dust.",{"by":"a Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock or Wizard","ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"],"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Staff of the Four Seasons","Staff","Very Rare",1,"A Quarterstaff with +2 to attack and damage rolls that changes with the seasons. It has 10 charges and regains 1d6 + 2 at dawn. While it has a charge, melee hits deal an extra 1d8 damage of the season's type: spring Radiant, summer Fire, autumn Necrotic, winter Cold. Spend 10 minutes to change the season for 8 hours. Spend charges to cast, using your spell save DC and attack modifier. **Spring.** Guiding Bolt (1), Moonbeam (2), Plant Growth (3). **Summer.** Burning Hands (1), Spike Growth (2), Fireball (3). **Autumn.** Inflict Wounds (1), Pass Without Trace (2), Vampiric Touch (3). **Winter.** Color Spray (1), Darkvision (2), Sleet Storm (3). If you spend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, it becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff.",{"by":"a Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock or Wizard","ch":[10,"1d6+2","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Staff of the Magpie","Staff","Rare",1,"A 10 lb stone staff topped with a magpie bust. Holding it gives +1 to Wisdom (Perception) checks to find treasure or a specific item. It has 10 charges and regains 1d6 + 4 at dawn. Spend charges to cast Fly (3) or Locate Object (2). If you spend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the magpie comes alive and flies off, leaving a nonmagical Quarterstaff.",{"by":"a spellcaster","ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"],"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Staff of the Mirage","Staff","Rare",1,"It has 10 charges and regains 1d6 + 4 at dawn. Spend charges to cast, using your spell save DC with a +2 bonus: Disguise Self (1), Hallucinatory Terrain (4), Invisibility (2), Mirror Image (2), Mislead (5) or Silent Image (1). If you spend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff vanishes.",{"by":"a Wizard","ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"],"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Staff of the Mustang","Staff","Rare",1,"A dark wooden staff carved as a stallion. It has 10 charges and regains 1d6 + 4 at dawn. Spend 1 charge to cast Phantom Steed. Spend 1 charge and a command word to Dash as a Bonus Action. If you spend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, it snaps in two and is destroyed, and galloping hooves fade into the distance.",{"ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"],"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Staff of the Reverent Warrior","Staff","Rare",1,"A Quarterstaff with +2 to attack and damage rolls, adorned with blades. Even unattuned, its attacks can deal Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing damage (your choice). It has 10 charges. While attuned you know True Strike, and when you cast it holding the staff you can spend charges to boost it. Spend 2 for a Bonus Action cast. Spend 1 to give the next attack roll against the target Advantage until the end of your next turn. On a hit, spend 1 for an extra 1d6 Radiant damage. It regains 1d6 + 4 at dawn. If you spend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, it becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff that still chooses its damage type.",{"by":"a spellcaster","ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Stalaga Spear","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A granite Spear with a ruby head that weighs as a normal Spear. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. It has 4 charges and regains 1d4 at dawn. Within 5 ft of unworked stone or earth, spend a Magic action and 1 charge to plunge it in. It erupts as a 1 ft wide, 10 ft long spike from another such surface within 60 ft you can see. Creatures in the 5 ft wide, 10 ft long Line make a DC 16 Dexterity save, taking 4d6 Piercing damage and being pushed 5 ft on a failure, or half damage on a success. Within 60 ft of the spike and 5 ft of stone or earth, recall the Spear as a Bonus Action with a command word.",{"ch":[4,"1d4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Spear"]}],["Starbreaker","Weapon","Rare",1,"A glowing Morningstar that sheds Bright Light in a 20 ft radius and Dim Light for 20 ft more. You gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls, and it deals an extra 1d4 Radiant damage. You can cast Daylight with it once per dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Morningstar"]}],["Starmetal Ring","Ring","Rare",0,"A rough ring with a pull on metal. Spend 1 hour touching an object (up to 25 lb, at least half metal) to bind it to the ring, one at a time. While wearing the ring, use a Bonus Action to pull the bound object up to 20 ft toward you if it is within 40 ft and not behind Cover. It bounces off creatures and objects on the way. If it reaches your space, you can catch it with a free hand or it drops at your feet.",{}],["Starmetal Shield","Armor","Legendary",1,"An open metal Shield that floats above its paired gauntlet. While wearing the gauntlet, you count as wielding the Shield but get +1 AC instead of the normal Shield bonus. The bonus is +3 against attacks made with a metal weapon or projectile. **Shooting Star.** As a Magic action, throw it at up to three creatures, objects or points. The first must be within 30 ft, and each next within 10 ft of the one before, with no repeats. Make a ranged attack against each, ignoring Cover. You are proficient and add Strength or Dexterity to attack and damage. A hit deals 2d8 Slashing damage. It returns to the gauntlet after the last target.",{"fx":{"ac":1},"base":["Shield"]}],["Starmetal Solar Axe","Weapon","Legendary",1,"An axe forged from star iron that is either one Greataxe (fused) or two Battleaxes (fissioned). **Fused.** +1 to attack and damage, an extra 2d6 Fire damage, and flames shed Bright Light in a 20 ft radius and Dim Light for 20 ft more, as sunlight. **Fissioned.** Each Battleaxe has +1 and an extra 1d6 Cold damage. They orbit you and count as sheathed. When you take the Attack action, a Bonus Action lets an orbiting axe attack a target within 20 ft. **Fission.** With a Bonus Action and a command word, split the Greataxe. Others within 30 ft make a DC 17 Dexterity save and take 3d6 Lightning damage, or half on a success. **Fusion.** With both axes held, a Bonus Action and another command word rejoin them. Others within 30 ft make a DC 17 Dexterity save and take 3d6 Fire damage, or half on a success. Each of these can be used only once per 12 hours.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Greataxe"]}],["Starmetal Striker","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Light Hammer forged from a comet, cold to the touch. You gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls, and it deals an extra 1d4 Cold damage. After a thrown attack it flies back to your hand, leaving a crackling mist.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Light Hammer"]}],["Steps of the Trickster","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Shoes that let you change the sound of your steps, though not the volume. You can make them sound like any material, such as bare feet, dancing heels or a guard's metal boots.",{}],["Storm Sickle","Weapon","Rare",0,"A Sickle that sparks and drips with water. Attacks deal an extra 1d4 Lightning damage. You can also slash the air to send a wind blade. You are proficient with it, the range is 20/60 ft, it uses Strength and deals 1d4 Slashing damage, and it gets the extra Lightning damage too.",{"base":["Sickle"]}],["Storm Thrower Harpoon","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A Trident with a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls. Thrown, it deals an extra 1d8 Lightning damage. After a throw, hit or miss, pull it back with its chain as a Bonus Action. After hitting a creature with it under open sky, call lightning. The target and each creature within 5 ft make a DC 16 Dexterity save and take 6d10 Lightning damage on a failure, or half on a success. Those in water or metal armor have Disadvantage, and you are immune to this lightning. Usable once until the next dawn. **Impale.** As a Magic action, make a ranged attack with it at a target no more than one size larger than you. On a hit, the target makes a DC 17 Strength save or is pulled up to 20 ft toward you.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3},"base":["Trident"]}],["Stormstruck Staff","Weapon","Rare",0,"A lightning-scarred Quarterstaff with a crystal at its head. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls, and it deals an extra 1 Lightning damage. When the staff takes Lightning damage, or you do while holding it (from another source), the crystal glows for 1 minute. It also glows under Shillelagh. While glowing it sheds Bright Light in a 10 ft radius and Dim Light for 10 ft more, and the extra Lightning damage becomes 1d6.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Sundersludge Net","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A Net made from a gray ooze. A creature Restrained by it takes 1d6 Acid damage when it gains the condition and at the end of each of its turns until freed. Nonmagical metal armor it wears takes a cumulative -1 AC penalty with each Acid hit and is destroyed when the AC would reach 10. Mending removes the penalty. Another creature that touches the Net takes 1d6 Acid damage. To escape, the target or an ally within 5 ft uses an action for a DC 13 Strength (Athletics) check. The Net (AC 10, 5 HP, Immunity to Bludgeoning, Poison and Psychic, Resistance to all other damage) frees the target if destroyed and is then harmless. If over half is saved and soaked in 5 gallons of liquid for 12 hours, it is repaired. Attunement ends if it stays torn over 48 hours. You are immune to its damage. A thrown Net is harmless until thrown again, and it does no Acid damage if nobody is attuned to it.",{}],["Switch","Rod","Very Rare",1,"A springy rod of vines. While holding it, spend a use of Wild Shape as a Bonus Action to turn it into any Simple or Martial weapon of your choice that deals Bludgeoning or Piercing damage and lacks Loading and Reach. A weapon with Ammunition makes its own. You are proficient with it and can use Wisdom for attack and damage. It deals an extra 1d8 damage of its type. A Bonus Action changes its form or returns it to a rod. Spend a second use of Wild Shape as a Magic action to cover yourself in bark. You gain Temporary Hit Points equal to four times your Druid level, and your AC is 17 if lower. It ends after hours equal to half your Druid level (round down), at 0 Hit Points, or early as a Bonus Action.",{"by":"a Druid"}],["Sword of Resonance","Weapon","Rare",1,"A brass Longsword with lute strings. It works as a Musical Instrument and a Spellcasting Focus, and you are proficient with it as both. You gain +2 to attack and damage rolls, and it has the Finesse property. When you spend Bardic Inspiration while holding it, it rings with thunder. Your next hit with it before the end of your next turn deals an extra 1d6 Thunder damage.",{"by":"a Bard","fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Longsword"]}],["Sword of the Spelldrinker","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A Longsword that drinks light. You gain a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls. Magical light and Darkness within 30 ft count as nonmagical, and you can breathe in any environment. It has 2 charges and regains 1d2 at dusk. Spend 1 to cast Counterspell. The target automatically fails if the spell is level 5 or lower and automatically succeeds against level 6+. When it works, you can absorb the spell instead (casting time of an action or Bonus Action), one at a time for 8 hours, replacing the old one. You can release it with a Magic action or Bonus Action to match its casting time, using the original caster's slot level, DC, attack bonus and ability.",{"ch":[2,"1d2","dusk"],"fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3},"base":["Longsword"]}],["Talyard the Great's Wand of Power","Wand","Uncommon",0,"A spruce stick that looks like a magnificent wand to anyone drunk who sees it. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 at dusk. While you are drunk and holding it, spend charges to cast (+3 spellcasting modifier): Heroism (1), Lesser Restoration (2) or Thaumaturgy (0).",{"ch":[3,"1d3","dusk"]}],["Tear of Gaia","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A small green gem. Crush it underfoot as a Magic action. Plants in a 10 ft Emanation from you become healthy and full, and fruit and vegetable plants bear produce that ripens over 1 hour. With no plants in range, or if crushed on inorganic ground, the area gets 1 inch of fertile topsoil and green grass.",{}],["Tectonic Gauntlets","Wondrous Item","Artifact",1,"Stone gauntlets with Earth's power. Your fist Unarmed Strikes deal 1d8 Bludgeoning damage (unless already higher) and double damage to objects and structures. They have 15 charges and regain 1d10 + 5 at dawn. On a fist Unarmed Strike, spend up to 5 charges to add 5 ft of reach per charge. **Powerglove.** On a hit, spend up to 3 charges for an extra 1d8 Bludgeoning damage each. If you spend any, the target makes a DC 18 Strength save or is pushed 5 ft. **Geomancy.** Cast with save DC 18: Earthquake (8), Move Earth (6), Shatter (2), Spike Growth (2, stone projections) or Wall of Stone (5). **Tectonic Plate Armor.** As a Magic action, for 1 hour you have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing, half Speed, and Disadvantage on Dexterity checks and saves. A Bonus Action ends it. You gain a 30 ft Burrow Speed through nonmagical, unworked earth and stone without disturbing it. If it ends while you are burrowed, you are shunted to the nearest free space and take 1d10 Force damage. Usable again after a Short or Long Rest. **Curse.** The gauntlets fuse to your flesh and cannot be removed. Your Speed drops by 5 ft and your Intelligence drops by 4 (minimum 7). The curse stays after attunement ends until Greater Restoration, Remove Curse or similar magic. **Random Properties.** One minor beneficial and one minor detrimental artifact property. **Destruction.** Only in the crystalline mines of Durhun on the Elemental Plane of Earth.",{"ch":[15,"1d10+5","dawn"]}],["Telescoping Bladelance","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A mechanical weapon you extend or retract with a Bonus Action by twisting the handle. Extended, it is a Lance. Retracted, it is a Greatsword that deals 1d10 Slashing damage instead of 2d6. While it is a Greatsword, you can extend it as a Bonus Action right after hitting. A Large or smaller target is then pushed 5 ft away.",{"base":["Lance"]}],["Tempest Griffon Feather Cape","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A cape that gives you Resistance to Lightning damage and Advantage on Dexterity saves against Lightning effects. As a Magic action with a command word, become a bolt of lightning and travel to an unoccupied space you can see within 120 ft without provoking Opportunity Attacks, filling a 5 ft wide Line along the path. Others in the Line, or within 5 ft of your old or new space, make a DC 16 Dexterity save and take 3d10 Lightning damage on a failure, or half on a success. Usable again after the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"res":["Lightning"]}}],["Tether Tearer","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A silver axe that pins a spirit to the material world. When you hit a creature with Incorporeal Movement, it takes an extra 1d6 Force damage and cannot use that trait until the end of its next turn.",{}],["Tethervine Quiver","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"An overgrown Quiver for up to 20 Arrows or Bolts that hides a plant. When you draw ammunition, use a Bonus Action and a command word to tie it to the vine. The vine trails the shot and becomes taut and climbable (holds 250 lb) if it hits a surface. While wearing the Quiver, retract the vine and its ammunition up to 60 ft as a Bonus Action. An object under 25 lb it hit comes along. If the ammunition hits a creature, the vine lets go and falls. A Bonus Action and the command word, or cutting it, also releases it. The vine reaches 120 ft, and the shot cannot go farther. A severed part regrows up to 30 ft each dawn, and the cut piece becomes mundane Rope.",{}],["The Griffon's Saddlebag","Wondrous Item","Artifact",0,"A leather bag with a griffon's face, made by the six-armed astral griffon Criir. It is usually found by an adventurer with a destiny. **Superior Holding.** Always 3 lb, it works as a Bag of Holding that only another Artifact can pierce. Placing a Bag of Holding, Heward's Handy Haversack, Portable Hole or similar item inside it, or the reverse, destroys the other item and moves its contents into the saddlebag. If that overloads it, random contents scatter in the Astral Plane. **Magic Courier.** At the GM's discretion, the beak opens to show a letter. Any creature with Intelligence 4+ can read it. It names an item and a person or place, with a price and a deadline. If brought in time, it hands over the item. If payment is not made within 1 hour, the item vanishes. After payment it gives the courier a reward. **Sell Magic Items.** Sell a magic item to it for half its base price. **Spells.** 8 charges, regains 1d6 + 2 at dawn. While wearing it, cast Detect Magic (1), Identify (1) or Legend Lore (5). The GM may unlock more: Blink (3), Dimension Door (4), Divination (4), Etherealness (7), Fly (3), Mordenkainen's Magnificent Mansion (7), Plane Shift (7) or Leomund's Secret Chest (4). **Sentience.** Chaotic Neutral, Int 13, Wis 15, Cha 16. Hearing and normal vision to 60 ft. It knows Common and speaks aloud among trusted creatures, otherwise telepathically with its wearer. It can talk with griffons. It likes to carry, collect and deliver magic items, and failed courier quests may make it withhold its magic, and items may be locked inside or spat out. **Destruction.** Piercing it with an Artifact sends it to its origin for repair, and it returns elsewhere. Putting one inside another sends both home and their contents to Criir's forge.",{"ch":[8,"1d6+2","dawn"]}],["The Rose Basket","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A silver Rapier with a rose on its guard and thorns on its hilt. You gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls. Against a Fey or a shape-shifted creature it deals an extra 1d8 Radiant damage. **Field of Roses.** As a Magic action with a command word, touch the point to the ground to raise silver rosebushes in a 25 ft square centered on you. It is Difficult Terrain for 1 minute or until you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. A creature takes 2d4 Piercing damage per 5 ft it moves in the area. You ignore the cost and the damage while holding the Rapier. Usable again after the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Rapier"]}],["Thornpiercer","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A rose with a stem you can hold as a hilt. As a Bonus Action, grow a Dagger, Shortsword, Rapier or Whip from its center. A new one replaces and withers the old. You gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls, an extra 1d4 Piercing damage on a hit, and proficiency with the grown weapons. **Dagger.** A thrown blade bursts into thorns on hit or miss. The target and up to three creatures of your choice within 10 ft make a DC 17 Dexterity save or take 1d4 + 2 Piercing damage. **Rapier.** On a roll of 20, the target takes an extra 10 Piercing damage. If it is Large or smaller, it makes a DC 17 Constitution save. On a failure its Hit Point maximum drops by the damage it took from the attack, and on a success by half that. This returns after a Short or Long Rest. **Shortsword.** The first creature you hit each turn makes a DC 17 Constitution save or takes 1d6 Poison damage and is Poisoned until the end of its next turn. **Whip.** When you hit a Medium or smaller creature, you can try to grapple it. It makes a DC 17 Strength save or is Grappled and takes 1d4 Piercing damage at the start of each of its turns. It or an ally within 5 ft can free it with an action and a DC 17 Strength (Athletics) check. The Whip breaks off from the hilt on a grapple so you can move freely.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2}}],["Thunderous Flail","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Flail with 3 charges that regains 1d3 at dawn. With at least 1 charge, the first target you hit each turn takes an extra 1d6 Lightning damage. Spend 1 charge to cast Thunderwave (save DC 15) from its ball, or as a Bonus Action right after a melee hit toward that target. The ball can be released mid-swing for a ranged attack. You are proficient, the range is 20/60 ft, it uses Strength and deals 1d8 Bludgeoning damage. While it is within 60 ft, pull it up to 20 ft toward you as a Bonus Action. It bounces off creatures and objects in the way, and reattaches when it enters your space. While detached, Thunderwave starts from the ball and fills a 10 ft radius Sphere centered on it.",{"ch":[3,"1d3","dawn"],"base":["Flail"]}],["Thwackstaff","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A festive Quarterstaff with ribbons that has the Finesse property. You get +1 to Charisma (Performance) checks to entertain with it. It has 3 charges and regains all at dawn. **Punishing Parry.** As a Reaction when a creature you see hits you with a melee attack, spend 1 charge and roll 1d6. Add it to your AC against that attack. If the attack misses, you can attack the attacker with the staff as part of the Reaction, and a hit deals extra damage equal to the number rolled.",{"ch":[3,"all","dawn"],"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Timber","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Handaxe whose power builds with each strike. Its bonus to attack and damage rolls equals its current charges. It gains 1 charge on each hit, up to 3. On the third, the energy explodes, charges reset, and the target takes an extra 3d6 Force damage, or 6d6 if made of wood. You can also push a target up to one size larger than you 10 ft. Charges last up to 1 minute and are lost if you miss, attack a different target, or attack with another weapon.",{"base":["Handaxe"]}],["Timepiercer","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A quartz sword hilt holding an hourglass whose sand never spills. As a Bonus Action with a command word, the sand forms a Rapier blade. A Bonus Action and the command word return it. While formed, you gain +2 to attack and damage rolls. While holding the hilt, cast Haste or Slow (save DC 16) from it, with Advantage on Constitution saves to keep Concentration on it. You can use each spell once until the next dawn. The sand speeds up with Haste and slows with Slow.",{"ch":[2,"2","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Rapier"]}],["Timeshifter's Mantle","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A cloak that bends time. When a Large or smaller creature hits you with a melee attack, take a Reaction. After the damage, move up to half your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks, and the attacker's Speed becomes 0 until the start of its next turn. Usable again after the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Toadstone","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A jade frog on a leather cord. You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed and can hold your breath for 1 hour. You can cast Jump on yourself once until the next dusk. **Curse.** Attuning curses you until Remove Curse or similar magic, and removing it does not help. Your skin stays damp and clammy, and you crave only insects and grubs.",{"ch":[1,"1","dusk"],"fx":{"swim":"walk"}}],["Tome of Dreams","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A book of gripping short stories. Read one in 10 minutes. After your next Long Rest, roll 1d20. On 10 or lower, you take 2d4 Psychic damage from terrors. On 11 or higher, you gain 2d4 Temporary Hit Points. An unfinished story has no effect.",{}],["Torchbearer's Reach","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A weapon with a magic flame on its handle that sheds Bright Light in a 20 ft radius and Dim Light for 20 ft more. Snap the handle (no action) to extend the flame into a 10 ft coil used as a Whip. It has the Light property and deals Fire damage instead of Slashing. The flame does not hurt you and cannot bind creatures or fetch objects, but it lights fires. A Bonus Action snuffs it.",{"base":["Whip"]}],["Torpedo Ammunition","Weapon","Common",0,"Spiral-shaped Arrows or Bolts. Fired underwater, they ignore the usual underwater combat penalties. Fired anywhere else, their normal and long range are halved.",{}],["Torrent Taiaha","Weapon","Rare",0,"A wooden staff circled by a mote of water, wielded as a Quarterstaff. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. You can lash out with the water for a special melee attack. You are proficient with it, the reach is 10 ft, you can use Wisdom for attack and damage, and it deals 1d4 Bludgeoning damage. The +1 applies to both forms. While holding it, you can walk on liquid as if solid, and you sink normally if you end your turn there. You can cast Control Water (only flood or part water) from it once until the next dawn, and it ends early if you let go.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Quarterstaff"]}],["Tote of Tricky Treat Sugarbombs","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A canvas bag holding 5d8 + 10 clove and pumpkin candies, with an illusory face on its pumpkin at night. Eat one as a Magic action and roll d20 for a minor effect that lasts 1 minute unless noted. 1: DC 13 Constitution save or lose your next action retching. 2: your face looks melted and skull-like (illusion). 3: food and water taste like ash and blood. 4: others' eyes look hollow and black. 5: your ears change color each turn. 6: your hair falls out and regrows. 7: maniacal laughter. 8: snake pupils. 9: an unseen fly buzzes. 10: orange skin, Bright Light 10 ft and Dim Light 10 ft more from eyes and mouth. 11: confetti and children's laughter. 12: tiny flightless bat wings. 13: you know the nearest pumpkin within 1 mile. 14: crows and ravens land on you. 15: a floppy wizard hat appears and fades in stars. 16: alcohol becomes nonalcoholic. 17: a golden voice, adding Proficiency to Charisma (Performance) to sing, or Expertise if already proficient. 18: food and water taste delicious. 19: Darkvision 30 ft, or +30 ft if you have it. 20: you sense possession and see Invisible creatures.",{}],["Trident of the Dryad","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A wooden Trident with 4 charges that regains 1d3 + 1 at dawn. Within 5 ft of a Large or bigger tree, spend a Bonus Action and 1 charge to teleport to a space within 5 ft of another such tree within 60 ft. **Tree Form.** As a Magic action with a command word, plant the base in fertile ground to turn it into a 60 ft tall tree with a 5 ft wide trunk and a 20 ft Emanation canopy. Within 5 ft of it, spend a Bonus Action and 1 charge to teleport to another point on its trunk or branches. It shows faint Transmutation to Detect Magic. Touch it and repeat the command word as a Magic action to revert, and creatures in it fall. Usable again after the next dawn.",{"ch":[4,"1d3+1","dawn"],"base":["Trident"]}],["Trident of the Hydra","Weapon","Rare",0,"A mithral Trident with a short handle that lacks the Versatile property. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. When you throw it, it splits into three spears and you make three ranged attacks instead of one. Each deals 1d6 Piercing damage and gets no ability modifier unless it is negative. Afterward it regrows its prongs from one spear and the other two dissolve.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Trident"]}],["Tub of Churning and Fermentation","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A tub holding 2 gallons of liquid or 1 cubic foot of material. Put in a liquid or perishable, close the lid and name an end product it can make. After 10 minutes it clicks open with the result. Examples: apples to hard cider, fruits to wine, cabbage to sauerkraut, cucumbers and vinegar to pickles, milk to butter, cheese or yogurt. Extra ingredients change the flavor. Usable again after the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Uorik the Conqueror's Juice Cup","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A brass cup. As a Bonus Action, whisper a fruit's name into it to give the water inside that fruit's juice color and flavor. Saying another fruit changes it again. It is still just water. Shouting into the cup makes it fizz. Poisoned water tastes foul and badly fermented.",{}],["Vancian Helm","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A helmet made from a shield guardian's remains. You gain +1 AC while wearing it. **Spell Storing.** Any creature can store a spell of level 1 to 4 by touching the helm as the spell is cast. It holds one spell at a time. While wearing it, you can cast that spell using the original caster's slot level, DC, attack bonus and ability, and the spell is then lost, as it is when a new one is stored. A level 5+ spell cast into it while worn is lost, the slot is spent, and you take 2d6 Psychic damage. Your eyes glow in a color of your choice while a spell is stored.",{"fx":{"ac":1}}],["Venombane Armor","Armor","Uncommon",1,"Any Light armor can be made this way. It absorbs poison and eases webs. You cannot be caught in webs and you move through them as Difficult Terrain. When you take Poison damage, use a Reaction to reduce it by 1d8 plus your Constitution modifier.",{}],["Vigilus","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Hand Crossbow with a spring case for six Bolts that loads itself, so you ignore its Loading property while the case has Bolts. A Utilize action reloads the case. As a Magic action, unfold three legs and plant it in your space as a Tiny turret. Within 30 ft of it, command it as a Bonus Action to attack a target you see within 30 ft of it, using your ability modifier. It draws and loads the next Bolt itself. The first creature that is Invisible (not you) to enter a space within 30 ft of it makes it chirp audibly out to 100 ft. It is an object with AC 12, HP 30 and Immunity to Poison and Psychic. At 0 HP it falls and cannot deploy for 1 minute. Retrieve it as a Bonus Action from its space.",{"base":["Hand Crossbow"]}],["Visage of Delight and Disaster","Wondrous Item","Legendary",1,"A mask that mirrors your expression. You gain two d10 Bardic Inspiration dice that work as the level 1 Bard feature and add to any you already have. You regain them after a Short or Long Rest. **Delight.** Given with a joyful performance, the creature has Advantage on saves to avoid or end Frightened for 1 minute. When it uses the die, it gains Temporary Hit Points equal to twice the roll. **Disaster.** Given with a grim performance, the creature has Advantage on saves to avoid or end Charmed for 1 minute. When it hits with a weapon or Unarmed Strike, it can spend the die to deal extra Psychic damage equal to twice the roll.",{"by":"a creature with Charisma 17 or higher"}],["Void Ammunition","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"Ammunition made of packed shadow. It deals Psychic damage instead of Piercing. It makes no sound, leaves no discernible wound, and vanishes after hitting or missing.",{}],["Volcanic Boots","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"Heavy volcanic stone boots that fit your feet and feel light and warm. You have Resistance to Fire damage. They have 10 charges and regain 1d6 + 4 at dawn. When you walk at least 5 ft on solid ground, spend charges as part of that movement. For each, choose an unoccupied space you passed through. A 5 ft Cube there turns volcanic and hot for 1 minute. A creature other than you that enters or starts its turn in one makes a DC 15 Dexterity save or takes 2d6 Fire damage. The Cubes revert if you are Unconscious, or early as a Bonus Action.",{"ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"],"fx":{"res":["Fire"]}}],["Volt Gauntlets","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Metal gauntlets with sharp knuckle points and insulated lining. Your fist Unarmed Strikes deal Piercing damage instead of Bludgeoning. They have 6 charges and regain 1d6 at dawn. With at least 1 charge, they give off sparks. When you hit with a fist Unarmed Strike, spend 1 charge for an extra 1d8 Lightning damage. The target also makes a DC 15 Constitution save or cannot make Opportunity Attacks until the start of its next turn.",{"ch":[6,"1d6","dawn"]}],["Voltedge","Weapon","Rare",1,"A split sword with electricity arcing between the halves. It deals an extra 1d6 Lightning damage on a hit. As a Magic action, fire a beam in a 60 ft long, 5 ft wide Line. Each creature in it makes a DC 15 Dexterity save and takes 4d6 Lightning damage on a failure, or half on a success. Usable again after the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Vox Helm","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A metal helm with a second guard over the mouth. With the guard down, your voice sounds obviously enchanted. You can change its pitch, masculinity or femininity, and echo at will with no action.",{}],["Wand of Whispers","Wand","Rare",1,"A wax and iron wand shaped like a candle on a candlestick, with a harmless flame that looks like candlelight. The flame sheds Bright Light in a 5 ft radius and Dim Light for 5 ft more. A Bonus Action lights or extinguishes it. It has 7 charges and regains 1d6 + 1 at dusk. Cast Message from it, or spend 3 charges for Sending. When you cast a level 0 to 5 spell while holding it, spend 1 charge per slot level to ignore its Verbal components. If you spend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the flame dies and it becomes a nonmagical candle and candlestick.",{"by":"a spellcaster","ch":[7,"1d6+1","dusk"]}],["War Standard of Battlecries","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",1,"A battle standard that stands 10 ft tall and folds to 2 ft. Extend it as a Magic action, then hold it up or plant it in an unoccupied space, and retrieve it by entering its space. While extended, you and allies within 15 ft of it at the start of combat gain +3 to Initiative. It has 4 charges and regains 1d4 at dawn. Within 15 ft of it, spend 1 charge and shout \"Charge!\" to Dash as a Bonus Action. Allies within 15 ft can Dash as a Bonus Action on their next turn. Change the emblem over 1 hour, even during a Short Rest.",{"ch":[4,"1d4","dawn"]}],["Warmind Wand","Wand","Rare",1,"A wand made from a warband leader's hilt and jawbone. It has 7 charges and regains 1d6 + 1 at dawn. If you spend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, it becomes a nonmagical sword hilt. **Forced Endurance.** Reaction, 2 charges: an ally within 30 ft who sees or hears you and is dropped to 0 Hit Points (not killed outright) drops to 1 instead. A creature can benefit once per Long Rest. **Form Ranks.** Magic action, 1 charge: an ally who sees or hears you gains 2d4 + 2 Temporary Hit Points and can use its Reaction to move half its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks. **Unyielding Critical.** Reaction, 1 charge: when an ally within 30 ft who sees or hears you scores a Critical Hit, add 2d4 to its damage roll. **Warband Strike.** When you take the Attack action, replace one attack and spend 1 charge. A willing creature who sees or hears you uses its Reaction to make one weapon or Unarmed Strike attack.",{"by":"an Orc","ch":[7,"1d6+1","dawn"]}],["Wavebender's Leiomano","Weapon","Rare",0,"A long oar edged with shark teeth. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. You can cast Control Water (only redirect flow) from it once until the next dawn, and it ends early if you let go. Rowing a waterborne vehicle with it adds 5 ft Speed (1/2 mile per hour) for each such oar used.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Glaive"]}],["Weapon of Mooring","Weapon","Rare",1,"A dense iron Battleaxe, Longsword or Warhammer with the Heavy property. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. A Large or smaller creature you hit has its Speed reduced by 5 ft until the end of its next turn.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1}}],["Weapon of Showmanship","Weapon","Common",0,"Any Simple or Martial weapon. When you reduce a Small or larger creature to 0 Hit Points, or score a Critical Hit, you can create a harmless sensory effect or illusion as in Prestidigitation, on the target or nearby.",{}],["Weapon of Spite","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A deep red Melee weapon made by a vengeful smith. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. Against a creature that has damaged you since the end of your last turn, the bonus is +2.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1}}],["Webgrip Rucksack","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A spiderskin bag with lifeless eyes that sometimes blink and a thin lining of sticky web. Items inside stay put, and other creatures have Disadvantage on Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks to steal from it while you wear it. Its eight straps stick to surfaces like your torso or a tavern wall. While worn, release them as a Magic action. Others have Disadvantage on Strength checks to wrench it from you. It holds 8 cubic feet or 80 lb and stretches a little to fit its contents.",{}],["Wildman's Spinning Cleaver","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Handaxe that channels bloodlust. You gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls. After a ranged attack, hit or miss, it flies back to your hand. Once per turn when you make a ranged attack with it while Raging, make a second ranged attack as part of it against a different target within 10 ft of the first, even beyond long range, treated as the first target's range. It flies back after the second.",{"by":"a Barbarian","fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Handaxe"]}],["Windrazor","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A Longsword with +2 to attack and damage rolls and the Finesse property. It has 10 charges and regains 1d6 + 4 at dawn. Cast with save DC 17 and +5 spell attack: Heroism (1) or Wind Wall (3). **Air Rend.** When you take the Attack action, replace one or more attacks, spending 1 charge each. Each is a special ranged attack against a target within 30 ft. **Sudden Storm.** As a Reaction when a creature within 5 ft damages you, spend 1 charge to make a melee attack with the sword against it. As a Reaction when a creature hits you with a ranged attack, spend 1 charge to cut the projectile and lower the total damage by 1d10 + 5. At 0 damage, a nonmagical projectile is destroyed.",{"ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Longsword"]}],["Windswept Wyvernplate","Armor","Rare",1,"Half Plate that grows lighter when you inhale. Hold your breath to lighten it and quiet it, which cancels its Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. If you fall while wearing it, hold your breath as a Reaction to cast Feather Fall on yourself.",{"base":["Half Plate Armor"]}],["Winter's Embrace","Armor","Very Rare",1,"Frosty Breastplate that keeps you at a comfortable temperature. You have Resistance to Cold and Fire damage, and ice or snow Difficult Terrain costs no extra movement. You can cast the level 6 Ice Storm (save DC 16) from it, centered on a point within 5 ft of you, and you are immune to its effects. Usable again after the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"res":["Cold","Fire"]},"base":["Breastplate"]}],["Wisplight Lantern","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A dark Hooded Lantern that needs no fuel and burns with a will-o'-wisp's blue flame. A Bonus Action sets its Bright Light radius from 5 to 20 ft, with Dim Light for the same distance beyond, or closes the hood for no light. It has 4 charges and regains 1d3 + 1 at dusk. As a Magic action, spend 1 charge and touch it to a Large or smaller corpse to see a ghostly illusion replay the last 6 seconds of its conscious life. It shows only the creature's actions, not the cause. It does not work on Undead, and a corpse can be shown once. Alternatively, spend 1 charge with a command word as a Magic action. If any Undead within 60 ft is not behind Cover, the light flashes red.",{"ch":[4,"1d3+1","dusk"]}],["Wooden Chain of the Unbroken Circle","Armor","Rare",1,"A Chain Shirt of wooden links enchanted by militant Druids. You gain a bonus to AC equal to your Wisdom modifier (maximum +2). You are trained with it even if you lack Medium armor training.",{"by":"a Druid or Ranger","base":["Chain Shirt"]}],["Wyvernwing","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Greatsword with a wyvern's wing stretched between three folding blades. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. It has 4 charges and regains 1d4 at dawn. As a Magic action, spend 1 charge to fan it open and swing down a buffeting wind in a 15 ft Cone or around you in 5 ft. Each affected creature makes a DC 15 Dexterity save and takes 2d6 Bludgeoning damage and is pushed up to 10 ft on a failure, or half damage on a success. It then folds closed.",{"ch":[4,"1d4","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Greatsword"]}],["Zafu of the Wandering Mind","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A set of stitched meditation pillows. Settling into meditation takes 1 minute. You can talk lightly but cannot move or take actions. While meditating you can levitate yourself and the pillows up to 5 ft. It ends if you take damage, leave the pillows, or choose to stop (no action). Within 100 ft of a pillow, use a Bonus Action and command word to send them into a pocket dimension, and repeat to return them to an open space within 5 ft. The set has 3 charges and regains 1d3 at dawn. While meditating, spend 1 charge to cast Arcane Eye without ending the meditation. If the meditation ends, your Concentration on the spell breaks.",{"by":"a Monk","ch":[3,"1d3","dawn"]}],["Fanfare Ammunition","Weapon","Common",0,"Trick ammunition meant to distract. On a ranged hit it deals no damage and is destroyed. A noise of your choice, from a whisper to a scream, sounds at the impact point. A creature that hears it can tell it is an illusion with a DC 10 Intelligence (Investigation) check.",{}],["Festerwood Masher","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Maul or Warhammer of corroded wood with +2 to attack and damage rolls. It has 3 charges and regains all at dusk. When you hit, spend 1 charge to splash acid. A Large or smaller target takes a cumulative -1 penalty to AC for 1 minute. A Huge target takes the penalty only from the second splash, and a Gargantuan one from the third, within 1 minute. When the hammer hits an affected target, it takes an extra 1d4 Acid damage per -1 of AC penalty.",{"ch":[3,"all","dusk"],"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Maul","Warhammer"]}],["Forgemaster's Might","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A Maul or Warhammer that needs Strength 17 or higher to wield. +2 to attack and damage rolls. As a Bonus Action, speak \"light the forge\" to wreathe the head in flames: Bright Light in 20 ft and Dim Light for 20 ft more, an extra 1d8 Fire damage on a hit, and it ignores Fire Resistance. Speak \"quench\" as a Bonus Action to end it, or drop or stow the hammer.\n**Smith's Blessing.** Cast Creation (level 6 version) or Fabricate as a Magic action, once each until the next dawn. Creation's materials can feed Fabricate. You know Mending while attuned, and it can repair a break or tear of up to 5 ft. You have Advantage on Smith's Tools checks to craft or repair an object using the hammer head as the anvil.\n**Iron Raze.** It deals an extra 2d8 Bludgeoning damage to Constructs and structures.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Maul","Warhammer"]}],["Galepierce Weapon","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Piercing weapon with the Thrown property, tempered to glide on wind. The normal and long ranges of its Thrown property double. Ranged attacks with it ignore air-based hindrances such as fog and strong winds, so they carry no Disadvantage or automatic miss from those causes.",{}],["Healing Ammunition","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"Ammunition made by elder nature clerics. A hit deals no damage. If the target is a creature other than you, it regains 2d4 Hit Points plus your Dexterity and Wisdom modifiers (minimum +1). You have Advantage on the attack roll against an ally. The ammunition dissolves into healing magic once it hits.",{}],["Memento of the Shapeless","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A Melee weapon forged from a mimic's remains. +2 to attack and damage rolls. As a Bonus Action, speak a command word to reshape it into any Melee weapon you are proficient with that lacks the Heavy and Reach properties.\n**Grapple.** When you hit, you can try to grapple the target at no action cost. It must succeed on a DC 13 Strength save or have the Grappled condition. While it lasts, you cannot attack or grapple another creature with the weapon. Releasing the weapon ends the condition.\n**Pseudopod.** As a Magic action, make a melee attack against a creature within 30 ft, ignoring Half Cover and Three-Quarters Cover. It deals 6d8 Bludgeoning damage on a hit. If you try to grapple with it, the save DC is 15. On a failure the target is pulled up to 15 ft toward you, or up to 30 ft and kept Grappled if it fails by 5 or more. After 12 hours you can use this again.\n**Limb Replacement.** If you miss an arm or forearm, you can graft the weapon in its place. You add your Proficiency Bonus to Strength (Athletics) checks with that limb, doubled if you are already proficient in Athletics. You can reshape the limb into the weapon or back at will.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2}}],["Moonswaddled Armor","Armor","Rare",0,"Light armor that gives +1 AC while worn between dusk and dawn. When you take a Short Rest after dusk, each Hit Point Die you spend restores its highest possible roll.",{}],["Phoenix Ammunition","Weapon","Rare",0,"An Arrow or Bolt fletched with phoenix feathers, bound to a Quiver or Crossbow Bolt Case. +1 to attack and damage rolls. A hit deals Fire damage instead of Piercing. At the start of your next turn it turns to ash and reappears in its container.\nAs a Bonus Action before firing, speak a command word to ignite it. If fired that turn, it deals an extra 1d6 Fire damage on a hit and turns to ash at once, or before reaching a target more than 30 ft away.\nThe container holds up to ten other Arrows or Bolts but only one Phoenix piece. If it is destroyed, it returns after 24 hours unless it was nonmagical when destroyed, such as inside an Antimagic Field.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1}}],["Runic Ammunition","Weapon","Rare",0,"Ammunition etched with runes that clash with spellcasting. +1 to attack and damage rolls. A concentrating creature it hits has Disadvantage on the save to keep Concentration. After it hits, it becomes nonmagical.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1}}]];
